1
00:01:40,288 --> 00:01:44,984
<i>Last year's world champion Beau Brandenburg
wins the first place in the new season.</i>

2
00:01:48,964 --> 00:01:53,547
<i>The big story at the Miami's Grand Prix
is the surprising second-place finish...</i>

3
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:56,237
<i>of unknown rookie Jimmy Bly.</i>

4
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:58,271
<i>Where did he come from?</i>

5
00:01:58,283 --> 00:01:59,968
<i>The racing world has
a new heartthrob.</i>

6
00:02:03,226 --> 00:02:05,068
<i>Bly, second place in England.</i>

7
00:02:05,069 --> 00:02:07,347
<i>Bly, becoming a serious contender.</i>

8
00:02:07,523 --> 00:02:09,313
<i>Jimmy Bly, he's a natural.</i>

9
00:02:09,675 --> 00:02:12,154
<i>We're in Rio for race six.</i>

10
00:02:13,612 --> 00:02:16,185
<i>A surprise win for rookie Jimmy Bly.</i>

11
00:02:18,158 --> 00:02:20,197
<i>Brandenburg's first loss of the season.</i>

12
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:23,347
<i>A second incredible upset.
Jimmy Bly wins in Michigan.</i>

13
00:02:23,422 --> 00:02:24,902
<i>Brandenburg loses again.</i>

14
00:02:26,158 --> 00:02:28,783
<i>We're down under for
the 11th race of the season.</i>

15
00:02:30,586 --> 00:02:32,543
<i>Brandenburg has lost three in a row.</i>

16
00:02:34,298 --> 00:02:38,069
<i>Bly and Brandenburg are a
dead tie in the championship.</i>

17
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:39,965
<i>Bly is starting to look nervous.</i>

18
00:02:40,138 --> 00:02:42,842
<i>- Cracks are starting to show.
- It's part of being a rookie.</i>

19
00:02:43,015 --> 00:02:47,013
<i>It'll be interesting to see how long
this young man can keep this up.</i>

20
00:03:29,352 --> 00:03:33,083
<i>Hey, Demille, you promised
a sound bite for tonight's sports!</i>

21
00:03:33,181 --> 00:03:36,351
Jimmy, only talk to this woman.
This reporter only.

22
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:01,581
Demille, can we call it?

23
00:04:02,133 --> 00:04:04,090
Wait a minute. Come here.

24
00:04:04,552 --> 00:04:06,545
Think. Let me explain something to you.

25
00:04:06,763 --> 00:04:09,089
These people love you, they buy tickets.

26
00:04:09,090 --> 00:04:11,433
The other people, the ones with
the cameras, they help sell tickets.

27
00:04:11,457 --> 00:04:13,766
- You know I need to think about tomorrow.
- This is tomorrow.

28
00:04:13,787 --> 00:04:15,646
This is part of the game.

29
00:04:15,813 --> 00:04:19,147
In five years, when you're
a brand name, you'll thank me.

30
00:04:59,105 --> 00:05:02,474
Beau, you've had problems before
and you've never acted like this.

31
00:05:03,593 --> 00:05:05,021
Things change.

32
00:05:05,695 --> 00:05:08,102
Why can't you just respect
what I need?

33
00:05:10,825 --> 00:05:13,078
You're having a bad season and
you're throwing me out of your life?

34
00:05:13,102 --> 00:05:14,530
This is my life!

35
00:05:15,037 --> 00:05:17,279
This is not your life!

36
00:05:20,109 --> 00:05:22,266
This is what you do for a living.

37
00:05:22,967 --> 00:05:24,277
Look...

38
00:05:26,312 --> 00:05:27,830
If I'm going to win...

39
00:05:27,865 --> 00:05:32,377
I need my mind out there, not here.
So right now this is my life.

40
00:05:34,723 --> 00:05:36,182
This is your life.

41
00:05:41,729 --> 00:05:43,307
What am I?

42
00:05:48,277 --> 00:05:49,606
What am I?

43
00:05:51,222 --> 00:05:52,816
A distraction.

44
00:05:54,684 --> 00:05:56,159
I'm sorry.

45
00:06:40,563 --> 00:06:44,618
<i>We're at number 193
of this 225 lap race.</i>

46
00:06:44,874 --> 00:06:48,325
<i>The defending world champion,
Beau Brandenburg, is in first place...</i>

47
00:06:48,586 --> 00:06:52,583
<i>driving better than we've
seen him drive all season long.</i>

48
00:06:53,256 --> 00:06:56,424
<i>Christian Fittipaldi in the
black car sits in second place.</i>

49
00:06:57,303 --> 00:07:00,469
<i>And the young rookie, Jimmy Bly,
sits back in third.</i>

50
00:07:00,681 --> 00:07:03,053
Bly's seems to have been shaky
for the last few races.

51
00:07:03,308 --> 00:07:06,225
<i>He's such a promising star,
just got raw talent.</i>

52
00:07:06,478 --> 00:07:09,099
<i>If Carl Henry could
get him to relax...</i>

53
00:07:11,024 --> 00:07:13,694
<i>there'll be no stopping him.</i>

54
00:07:14,903 --> 00:07:17,773
<i>Laps wind down.
It's a very tight panel at the front.</i>

55
00:07:20,658 --> 00:07:24,193
<i>Bly tries to make his move now
on the number 11 of Fittipaldi.</i>

56
00:07:24,453 --> 00:07:26,910
<i>Motorola car comes to the inside.</i>

57
00:07:31,794 --> 00:07:35,360
<i>And he does it!
Sweet pass by the rookie, Bly.</i>

58
00:07:35,395 --> 00:07:36,675
Great. You're doing great.

59
00:07:37,299 --> 00:07:40,715
<i>Close on Brandenburg?
Everybody wants to know that.</i>

60
00:07:41,136 --> 00:07:43,323
<i>Bly really seems to be
having a problem with</i>

61
00:07:43,335 --> 00:07:45,680
<i>consistency and focus on
this race track today.</i>

62
00:07:45,933 --> 00:07:49,099
<i>Even so, he now finds himself
in second place.</i>

63
00:07:51,355 --> 00:07:54,106
<i>With just 10 laps to go,
Brandenburg leads.</i>

64
00:07:54,316 --> 00:07:57,006
<i>Oh, you're looking good.
Looking good right there.</i>

65
00:07:58,612 --> 00:08:00,353
<i>Brandenburg's experience
is showing through</i>

66
00:08:00,365 --> 00:08:02,277
<i>here today. He knows how
to take those corners.</i>

67
00:08:02,491 --> 00:08:06,025
<i>Jimmy Bly coming into the corner
has a tendency to slow down.</i>

68
00:08:08,371 --> 00:08:10,329
<i>A lot of pressure on young Bly.</i>

69
00:08:10,330 --> 00:08:11,921
Pass for chrissake!

70
00:08:12,416 --> 00:08:13,828
<i>What is he afraid of?</i>

71
00:08:14,085 --> 00:08:17,121
<i>Follow Brandenburg's line.
Are you following Brandenburg's line?</i>

72
00:08:17,547 --> 00:08:19,954
I can't follow his line.
Can I pick another line?

73
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:21,959
Take Brandenburg's line.

74
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:26,045
<i>Bly drafts up into the vacuum
behind Brandenburg's car.</i>

75
00:08:26,305 --> 00:08:30,255
<i>But every time he steps out of that
vacuum he runs into a wall of air.</i>

76
00:08:30,476 --> 00:08:32,883
<i>That slows him down,
that affects his momentum.</i>

77
00:08:32,884 --> 00:08:35,273
<i>Lay it out, Jimmy. Lay it out.</i>

78
00:08:35,308 --> 00:08:38,807
<i>You better win this thing.
Win it or you're gonna look a damn fool.</i>

79
00:08:41,403 --> 00:08:44,653
<i>Bly down to the inside,
tries to get alongside him!</i>

80
00:08:44,864 --> 00:08:47,736
<i>Very, very close as they
come off at the corner.</i>

81
00:08:59,128 --> 00:09:02,379
<i>Can Bly get past him here?
It's gonna be close.</i>

82
00:09:02,675 --> 00:09:05,714
Son of a bitch, not again.
He's gone.

83
00:09:06,344 --> 00:09:09,428
<i>Bly makes his move,
nails the throttle.</i>

84
00:09:11,766 --> 00:09:13,722
<i>They touch and Bly's in trouble!</i>

85
00:09:13,892 --> 00:09:16,976
<i>Can he keep it off the wall?
He slides down to the inside.</i>

86
00:09:17,187 --> 00:09:20,521
<i>Bly's spinning out of control.</i>

87
00:09:36,915 --> 00:09:38,374
<i>Damn it!</i>

88
00:09:38,667 --> 00:09:42,401
<i>And it gives the win over
to the defending world champion.</i>

89
00:09:42,687 --> 00:09:46,086
<i>This is Beau Brandenburg's day.</i>

90
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:53,553
<i>This is Beau Brandenburg's
first victory in three races.</i>

91
00:09:53,565 --> 00:09:55,342
<i>He's gotta be happy about that.</i>

92
00:09:55,558 --> 00:09:59,935
<i>Brandenburg's back in the lead in
the race for the world championship.</i>

93
00:10:05,067 --> 00:10:08,021
Crusher, it's time
to call Joe Tanto.

94
00:10:39,934 --> 00:10:40,966
Hello?

95
00:10:42,895 --> 00:10:45,517
Your day won't come when
you're up before me, old friend.

96
00:10:47,191 --> 00:10:48,519
How are you doing, Carl?

97
00:10:50,235 --> 00:10:51,235
I was just...

98
00:10:52,112 --> 00:10:53,606
feeling nostalgic.

99
00:10:55,825 --> 00:10:57,153
You still there?

100
00:10:57,268 --> 00:10:59,800
You think you can you
push it to the ragged edge?

101
00:10:59,801 --> 00:11:01,146
Yeah, I think so.

102
00:11:01,372 --> 00:11:03,613
- And the fear?
- It's gone.

103
00:11:04,082 --> 00:11:06,917
- Fear's never gone.
- Yeah, maybe.

104
00:11:09,629 --> 00:11:12,121
- What about Memo?
- I'm making a change.

105
00:11:12,382 --> 00:11:15,004
Memo's out, you're in.

106
00:11:15,218 --> 00:11:17,511
You're driving for me again, Joseph.

107
00:11:17,512 --> 00:11:19,551
Welcome back to the big show.

108
00:11:27,772 --> 00:11:29,537
So what do you think is going on, Jimmy?

109
00:11:29,572 --> 00:11:32,452
Because this bad thing you're going
through is coming at a very bad time.

110
00:11:33,027 --> 00:11:35,482
- So talk to me.
- I said, it's nothing.

111
00:11:35,946 --> 00:11:38,238
What is it?
What am I, a piece of wood?

112
00:11:38,949 --> 00:11:41,882
- I'm talking to you!
- Look, I can't do this.

113
00:11:41,917 --> 00:11:45,238
I can't handle it. They're pulling me in
10 different directions at the same time.

114
00:11:45,623 --> 00:11:48,493
I thought I could handle it,
but I can't.

115
00:11:48,667 --> 00:11:50,839
You can, and you will.

116
00:11:50,911 --> 00:11:53,225
Wait a minute. I don't care, if
you're pulled in a 100 directions.

117
00:11:53,226 --> 00:11:54,706
We deal with it. Okay?

118
00:11:54,741 --> 00:11:57,086
Well, then stop pushing on
me like you're one of them.

119
00:11:57,342 --> 00:11:59,668
Wait. "Them"?

120
00:12:00,554 --> 00:12:02,630
Like I'm the enemy? "Them"?

121
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,766
That's great. That's...

122
00:12:08,770 --> 00:12:12,185
You know from day 1 when you started
kicking my ass on everything with wheels...

123
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:15,768
It's been us. I said my brother
has the touch, I don't. That's fine.

124
00:12:16,027 --> 00:12:18,352
But what I do have
is allegiance to you.

125
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:20,736
So don't doubt me. Don't do that.

126
00:12:22,783 --> 00:12:26,615
I saw this 8-year-old,
goofy-looking kid...

127
00:12:26,787 --> 00:12:31,414
on a piece of junk go-cart,
come from three laps behind...

128
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:33,541
to beat guys twice his age.

129
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:37,578
You rebounded then, right?

130
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:39,458
We'll rebound now.

131
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:43,086
Everybody trips. That's okay.
That's life.

132
00:12:43,261 --> 00:12:45,467
It's how fast you get up that counts.

133
00:12:46,389 --> 00:12:48,014
So get up, Jimmy.

134
00:12:49,017 --> 00:12:50,844
But get up fast.

135
00:13:14,166 --> 00:13:18,246
We just got word from Carl Henry
that Joe "The Hummer" Tanto...

136
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:20,045
will be replacing Memo Moreno...

137
00:13:20,248 --> 00:13:23,456
as Jimmy Bly's teammate
in the Toronto Molson Indy.

138
00:13:57,875 --> 00:13:59,073
Excuse me.

139
00:14:00,252 --> 00:14:02,577
How about an autograph, cold fish?

140
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:06,295
- What are you doing back here, Joe?
- I'm glad to see you're warm as always.

141
00:14:06,508 --> 00:14:09,404
I've talked to the team. I guess they
figured you needed some competition.

142
00:14:09,428 --> 00:14:11,635
Now there's a familiar face.
Sophia!

143
00:14:12,056 --> 00:14:13,550
Joe, don't call her, please.

144
00:14:14,350 --> 00:14:15,350
What's wrong?

145
00:14:16,643 --> 00:14:18,617
- Joe...
- Still working here, huh?

146
00:14:18,728 --> 00:14:22,014
- We haven't seen you in a long time.
- No, no, no.

147
00:14:22,032 --> 00:14:24,106
So, you keeping this guy under control?

148
00:14:24,318 --> 00:14:25,229
<i>You driving?</i>

149
00:14:25,230 --> 00:14:27,764
<i>Yeah, can you believe it.
I'm back with Carl Henry's team.</i>

150
00:14:27,799 --> 00:14:29,444
- Wow.
- Yeah.

151
00:14:29,614 --> 00:14:30,895
That's great.

152
00:14:33,201 --> 00:14:34,363
<i>Well...</i>

153
00:14:37,288 --> 00:14:39,116
I'll see you around, Joe.

154
00:14:42,085 --> 00:14:44,290
I think she wants to kill you.
What happened?

155
00:14:44,391 --> 00:14:45,591
Nothing.

156
00:14:45,671 --> 00:14:46,703
Nothing?

157
00:14:46,923 --> 00:14:49,413
So they really put you in a car again.
Why?

158
00:14:49,592 --> 00:14:51,383
All you do now is get in the way.

159
00:14:51,593 --> 00:14:54,547
- Somebody must think I got something left.
- Somebody?

160
00:14:54,721 --> 00:14:56,003
- Yeah.
- What do you think?

161
00:14:56,224 --> 00:14:58,148
Me. I think it's will over skill.

162
00:14:58,225 --> 00:15:00,930
Will over skill?
Like in Detroit in '97?

163
00:15:01,854 --> 00:15:04,345
- Hey, accidents happen.
- Accidents?

164
00:15:05,190 --> 00:15:06,565
You almost killed me, Joe.

165
00:15:06,775 --> 00:15:10,393
You know, Beau, I'm just
glad I'm back. I really am.

166
00:15:12,698 --> 00:15:15,105
- It's a different time. I'm different.
- You...

167
00:15:15,367 --> 00:15:17,110
will never be different.

168
00:15:17,327 --> 00:15:19,533
Be seeing you in my rear-view, Joe.

169
00:15:21,706 --> 00:15:23,200
- Excuse me.
- Yeah.

170
00:15:23,541 --> 00:15:25,996
Please, picture. Please.

171
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:27,622
Picture? No problem.

172
00:15:30,715 --> 00:15:32,838
You gotta be kidding, right?

173
00:15:37,263 --> 00:15:38,377
Smile.

174
00:15:41,266 --> 00:15:42,429
How you doing, guys?

175
00:15:42,643 --> 00:15:44,102
- Joseph.
- Carl.

176
00:15:45,104 --> 00:15:47,097
I want you to meet our sponsors.

177
00:15:47,481 --> 00:15:49,308
You've been gone a while, Joe.

178
00:15:49,525 --> 00:15:52,276
He hasn't really be gone.
Been up north testing cars for us.

179
00:15:52,444 --> 00:15:54,271
Shouldn't he be wearing one of our hats?

180
00:15:55,639 --> 00:15:57,897
It's a little damp, isn't it?

181
00:15:58,158 --> 00:15:59,357
- Just kidding.
- I'm sorry.

182
00:15:59,577 --> 00:16:02,150
- This is Lucretia Jones.
- Hi.

183
00:16:02,371 --> 00:16:04,811
- How are you doing?
- Most people do better calling me "Luc."

184
00:16:04,873 --> 00:16:06,782
Luc? I think I can remember that.

185
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,800
Miss Jones is a journalist. She's
gonna be with the rest of the season.

186
00:16:10,003 --> 00:16:13,087
She's doing an expos�
on male dominance in sport.

187
00:16:13,256 --> 00:16:15,200
Do you have any free time
to get together to talk?

188
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:17,954
Well, you gotta ask the legend here.
Whatever he wants, good by me.

189
00:16:17,989 --> 00:16:19,801
He always has free time
for a beautiful lady.

190
00:16:20,346 --> 00:16:23,513
- No speeding tickets, Joseph?
- No, no speeding tickets.

191
00:16:23,683 --> 00:16:25,225
- Bye.
- Bye.

192
00:16:25,434 --> 00:16:27,676
- Nice to meet you.
- See you later, Luc.

193
00:16:27,895 --> 00:16:30,018
Give him hell, Joe.

194
00:16:30,839 --> 00:16:33,248
I thought Tanto was dead,
for chrissake.

195
00:16:35,778 --> 00:16:37,153
Whoa!

196
00:16:38,364 --> 00:16:40,023
Now that ex-wife of yours...

197
00:16:40,574 --> 00:16:42,448
that's a piece of work.

198
00:16:43,018 --> 00:16:46,818
Divorces you and marries
a fellow driver.

199
00:16:47,122 --> 00:16:49,684
You know being back here makes me
realize how much I didn't miss you.

200
00:16:49,708 --> 00:16:51,451
- You missed me.
- Next subject.

201
00:16:51,668 --> 00:16:55,333
I got a rookie driver. His name
is Jimmy Bly. He's won five races.

202
00:16:55,589 --> 00:16:57,795
He's starting to find ways to stumble.

203
00:16:58,007 --> 00:17:00,628
I'm not going to lose that kind of lead.
It's not going to happen.

204
00:17:00,743 --> 00:17:02,895
Well you know Memo's a
great driver. What happened?

205
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:04,734
Memo forgot his damn job.

206
00:17:04,769 --> 00:17:09,264
His job is to support the team. His job
is to support Jimmy Bly. So he's gone.

207
00:17:09,477 --> 00:17:12,394
I could have hired a 100 young
Turks to take his place...

208
00:17:12,563 --> 00:17:15,019
but I wanted somebody who's
been to the top of the mountain...

209
00:17:15,274 --> 00:17:19,223
- and stumbled all the way to the bottom.
- Thanks for reminding me.

210
00:17:19,486 --> 00:17:22,986
I wanted somebody that...
gets his attention.

211
00:17:23,157 --> 00:17:24,865
- Maybe gains his trust.
- Why trust?

212
00:17:25,117 --> 00:17:27,323
Because you're gonna help him...

213
00:17:27,828 --> 00:17:31,113
- my old friend.
- Carl.

214
00:17:32,415 --> 00:17:35,867
Look. I gotta get something straight.
I thought you brought me back here to race.

215
00:17:36,128 --> 00:17:37,539
No.

216
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:39,374
- I'm gone.
- No, you're not.

217
00:17:39,548 --> 00:17:42,418
I'm not finished yet.
We go back.

218
00:17:44,010 --> 00:17:45,884
We go way back.

219
00:17:46,137 --> 00:17:50,217
I carried you for six years.
You owe me, Joe.

220
00:17:51,768 --> 00:17:53,891
All you gotta do is help this kid.

221
00:17:54,104 --> 00:17:56,476
Who knows? You might enjoy it.

222
00:17:56,689 --> 00:17:58,848
You got one offer on the table.

223
00:17:59,901 --> 00:18:01,525
Your choice.

224
00:18:10,286 --> 00:18:12,658
- What did you give him?
- Gas money.

225
00:18:23,256 --> 00:18:27,385
There are a hundred guys more
qualified to back Jimmy. Why him?

226
00:18:27,594 --> 00:18:31,592
Because when he's on, he's
one of the best you'll ever see.

227
00:18:31,765 --> 00:18:33,307
Just sit back and watch.

228
00:18:42,317 --> 00:18:43,396
What's he doing?

229
00:18:44,903 --> 00:18:48,069
He's just wound up.
Doing his coin bit will relax him.

230
00:18:49,949 --> 00:18:53,115
- What's his coin bit?
- He's gonna hold a control slide...

231
00:18:53,369 --> 00:18:56,370
going full out, then he's gonna
drift over to pick up three coins.

232
00:18:57,915 --> 00:19:00,620
Not with the front tire, mind you.
Any fool can do that.

233
00:19:00,835 --> 00:19:02,430
But he'll slide over and
snatch them up with

234
00:19:02,442 --> 00:19:04,242
the back one and not
losing millisecond speed.

235
00:19:04,338 --> 00:19:07,125
- There's no way he can do that.
- You don't want to bet me.

236
00:19:24,899 --> 00:19:26,477
There's number one.

237
00:19:37,995 --> 00:19:38,995
There's number two.

238
00:19:45,628 --> 00:19:46,873
What's that sound?

239
00:19:49,381 --> 00:19:52,086
- It sounds like humming.
- Yep.

240
00:19:52,301 --> 00:19:53,380
Why is he humming?

241
00:19:53,886 --> 00:19:57,634
Just some crazy thing he does
when he's pushing close to the edge.

242
00:19:58,056 --> 00:20:01,176
- Anyone else ever do that?
- Not among the living.

243
00:20:14,741 --> 00:20:18,150
- You want to back it off, Joe?
- Let him go.

244
00:20:18,368 --> 00:20:20,444
I want to see if he's still got it.

245
00:20:36,552 --> 00:20:40,217
Well, I think you passed the audition, and
I'm not mopping up the mess, Hummer.

246
00:20:51,358 --> 00:20:53,018
Not bad, Hummer.

247
00:21:03,661 --> 00:21:06,746
- Your humming is getting better.
- That means you gonna let me drive again?

248
00:21:06,957 --> 00:21:09,957
No I said your humming was
getting better, not your driving.

249
00:21:11,669 --> 00:21:13,377
Go talk to the kid.

250
00:21:20,177 --> 00:21:21,886
How you doing? I'm Joe.

251
00:21:22,096 --> 00:21:24,504
- How you doing. Nice run out there.
- Nice. It was okay.

252
00:21:25,975 --> 00:21:28,679
Hey, listen, I liked Memo.

253
00:21:29,478 --> 00:21:31,470
He's a good guy, good driver.

254
00:21:31,730 --> 00:21:34,399
Just to let you know.
We didn't have any problems at all.

255
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:39,898
Two out of three, huh?

256
00:21:42,282 --> 00:21:47,620
Jimmy, why don't you and me grab a cup
of coffee and maybe talk some strategy?

257
00:21:48,496 --> 00:21:52,244
The strategy's simple: He drives,
you block. You block, he wins.

258
00:21:52,416 --> 00:21:54,742
Look. We gotta hit it.
We got a big time publicity blitz.

259
00:21:54,961 --> 00:21:56,242
Try to push that back, can't you?

260
00:21:56,263 --> 00:21:58,953
Come on buddy.
Part of the gig, part of the contract.

261
00:21:59,549 --> 00:22:01,091
Talk to you later.

262
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:04,550
You got anything, just channel
through me, ok? I channel well.

263
00:22:05,846 --> 00:22:07,257
Appreciate that.

264
00:22:13,104 --> 00:22:14,646
<i>Car coming down.</i>

265
00:22:25,850 --> 00:22:29,449
<i>In the racing world last week was Jimmy
Bly's close encounter with the wall.</i>

266
00:22:29,661 --> 00:22:33,445
<i>Bly was trailing Beau Brandenburg
on turn four of the last lap...</i>

267
00:22:33,665 --> 00:22:36,535
<i>when he lost control
at over 200 miles an hour.</i>

268
00:22:36,709 --> 00:22:39,663
<i>I don't know what's going on
with Bly's driving.</i>

269
00:22:39,837 --> 00:22:43,705
<i>It went so well earlier in the season,
surprising everyone.</i>

270
00:22:43,925 --> 00:22:46,630
<i>He can't seem to
get it together on the track.</i>

271
00:22:46,886 --> 00:22:50,634
<i>All eyes will be on Bly
at tomorrow's Toronto Grand Prix...</i>

272
00:23:35,016 --> 00:23:38,716
So, Luc, what have you learned
since you've been here?

273
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:42,073
Well actually, I used to think you just put
gas in the car and then push the pedal...

274
00:23:42,074 --> 00:23:44,409
Fuel. Get it right.

275
00:23:44,444 --> 00:23:46,151
Fuel. I knew that.

276
00:23:47,195 --> 00:23:49,670
Put the fuel in the car
and push the pedal...

277
00:23:49,688 --> 00:23:51,017
and that was it.

278
00:23:51,198 --> 00:23:53,736
Now that is embarrassing,
that's what that is.

279
00:23:53,951 --> 00:23:56,406
So Joe, with only 10 races
left in the season...

280
00:23:56,662 --> 00:23:59,152
why'd they bring you back?
What makes you so special?

281
00:23:59,372 --> 00:24:01,330
Oh, special I'm not.

282
00:24:03,085 --> 00:24:05,410
Do you feel awkward being back?

283
00:24:08,048 --> 00:24:09,931
Is there something you're
not telling me, Luc?

284
00:24:09,932 --> 00:24:14,452
Well, you know rumor has it you were...
quite the wild man of the circuit.

285
00:24:14,971 --> 00:24:17,051
I also heard you were married
to a woman named Cathy.

286
00:24:17,224 --> 00:24:19,928
You cleaned up your act, stopped
living your old lifestyle...

287
00:24:20,101 --> 00:24:22,094
but things just didn't work out.

288
00:24:22,562 --> 00:24:24,807
That's an interesting story
if it wasn't about me.

289
00:24:24,808 --> 00:24:27,358
I'm just relating what I heard, Joe.
I'm not trying to upset you.

290
00:24:27,382 --> 00:24:28,556
I guess this game's over.

291
00:24:29,026 --> 00:24:32,197
I wanted to interview you because
you actually have something to say.

292
00:24:32,198 --> 00:24:34,986
These young drivers they've barely lived.

293
00:24:35,021 --> 00:24:37,670
I mean your life is so colorful
by comparison.

294
00:24:37,705 --> 00:24:39,466
You know, Luc, if I was
trying to get to know you

295
00:24:39,467 --> 00:24:41,253
I won't remind you
what a fool you've been...

296
00:24:41,288 --> 00:24:45,124
and then insult you
by calling it colorful.

297
00:24:49,255 --> 00:24:50,465
I'm sorry.

298
00:24:50,466 --> 00:24:53,257
So don't judge me until you get
to know me a bit better, ok?

299
00:24:53,842 --> 00:24:54,923
How do I do that?

300
00:24:54,924 --> 00:24:58,062
Well you can start by
finishing this game, wise ass.

301
00:24:58,596 --> 00:25:01,597
Wise ass? Right.

302
00:25:01,975 --> 00:25:03,006
Good luck.

303
00:25:16,614 --> 00:25:17,614
Hi.

304
00:25:18,699 --> 00:25:19,699
Hi.

305
00:25:22,370 --> 00:25:25,406
- So.
- So.

306
00:25:27,792 --> 00:25:31,041
I heard about you and Beau.
And I'm sorry.

307
00:25:32,296 --> 00:25:33,671
Thanks.

308
00:25:34,589 --> 00:25:36,297
It's my problem.

309
00:25:36,508 --> 00:25:38,834
I'm sorry, Sophia.
I didn't mean to...

310
00:25:39,011 --> 00:25:40,754
get into your business.

311
00:25:43,598 --> 00:25:44,843
I'm trying to talk.

312
00:25:47,936 --> 00:25:50,771
Jimmy, I just came out of
a three-year relationship.

313
00:25:51,038 --> 00:25:53,609
- That's a long time.
- Yeah, it's a long time.

314
00:25:54,901 --> 00:25:57,736
When you get used to being
around someone, it's not...

315
00:26:00,615 --> 00:26:01,895
I don't know.

316
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:05,654
What?

317
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:12,955
- I shouldn't be here.
- Wait. No.

318
00:26:13,169 --> 00:26:16,869
- I shouldn't be doing this.
- Sophia, please.

319
00:26:17,881 --> 00:26:18,881
Stay.

320
00:26:27,099 --> 00:26:29,056
I'm not looking to get involved.

321
00:26:30,018 --> 00:26:32,177
I'm not over him.

322
00:26:32,354 --> 00:26:35,473
I understand that, Sophia.
I'm just looking for a friend.

323
00:26:35,982 --> 00:26:37,262
You sure?

324
00:26:38,693 --> 00:26:41,148
- Yeah. I think so.
- Think?

325
00:26:45,116 --> 00:26:47,821
Do you want to go sit down,
talk for a while?

326
00:26:49,203 --> 00:26:51,955
Yeah. Yeah, I would.

327
00:26:55,918 --> 00:27:00,046
<i>Welcome to Toronto, Canada, this year's
running of the Toronto Molson Indy...</i>

328
00:27:00,298 --> 00:27:03,085
<i>and ESPN's live coverage
of this incredible race.</i>

329
00:27:03,342 --> 00:27:05,631
- Hi, I'm Jeff Oaken.
- And I'm Dave Wershafter.

330
00:27:05,844 --> 00:27:09,758
<i>And this is race day
beside the lake.</i>

331
00:27:11,475 --> 00:27:12,554
<i>Because it is time.</i>

332
00:27:13,226 --> 00:27:16,232
<i>All the qualifying is done
and practicing is done...</i>

333
00:27:16,305 --> 00:27:20,019
<i>and now it's time to play the
cards and see how it goes down.</i>

334
00:27:35,832 --> 00:27:38,619
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome today's drivers,</i>

335
00:27:38,876 --> 00:27:41,101
<i>Max Papis, Joe Tanto...</i>

336
00:27:41,545 --> 00:27:43,787
<i>Jimmy Bly, Beau Brandenburg...</i>

337
00:27:44,840 --> 00:27:47,562
<i>This race is being watched
by millions around the world...</i>

338
00:27:47,735 --> 00:27:49,462
<i>from Finland to Australia.</i>

339
00:27:50,513 --> 00:27:54,128
<i>Over 250,000 people are expected
here in Toronto alone...</i>

340
00:27:54,241 --> 00:27:57,676
<i>from all over the world.
A 110 lap race on a street track.</i>

341
00:27:57,894 --> 00:28:00,916
<i>A lot of different styles of race tracks,
but the street track...</i>

342
00:28:00,972 --> 00:28:03,690
<i>is considered as being
the most hazardous.</i>

343
00:28:03,943 --> 00:28:07,477
<i>And that's because it takes place
on ordinary city streets.</i>

344
00:28:07,696 --> 00:28:12,357
<i>You guys here in Toronto
should be the loudest folks to cheer.</i>

345
00:28:12,701 --> 00:28:14,610
Well, well, well.

346
00:28:15,703 --> 00:28:18,160
So, what about me?

347
00:28:19,124 --> 00:28:20,998
How do I look?

348
00:28:21,167 --> 00:28:24,287
Or do you still hate answering
loaded questions?

349
00:28:25,546 --> 00:28:27,503
Go ahead, ask me.

350
00:28:27,965 --> 00:28:30,752
- You love him?
- I love a lot of things.

351
00:28:31,051 --> 00:28:33,459
- Why did you marry him?
- He's a younger, better you.

352
00:28:34,931 --> 00:28:35,962
Ouch.

353
00:28:36,641 --> 00:28:38,847
- You want to know more?
- No.

354
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:43,393
You left me.
With nothing, I might add.

355
00:28:43,405 --> 00:28:45,939
Just as Memo and I are
trying to get something

356
00:28:45,951 --> 00:28:48,443
together, yet you come
back to steal his job.

357
00:28:48,693 --> 00:28:51,466
And he still likes you.
How pathetic is that?

358
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:54,115
I'm sorry. I don't understand this
"brotherhood of speed" crap.

359
00:28:54,366 --> 00:28:56,240
Just answer me one question.

360
00:28:56,660 --> 00:29:00,740
Does hurting me make you feel better about
yourself, or that just comes naturally?

361
00:29:07,004 --> 00:29:11,048
You think you were better than me.
You weren't.

362
00:29:15,761 --> 00:29:17,090
Hey.

363
00:29:21,100 --> 00:29:22,808
- Joe.
- Memo.

364
00:29:23,061 --> 00:29:25,433
Hey, did Cathy say anything bad?

365
00:29:25,646 --> 00:29:29,264
She better not. Look at you.
How you been, good? Huh?

366
00:29:29,483 --> 00:29:31,392
Hey listen, I'm sorry about all this.

367
00:29:31,568 --> 00:29:34,142
Somebody had to take my ride,
why not an old friend?

368
00:29:34,363 --> 00:29:35,905
Great. That makes it even worse.

369
00:29:36,406 --> 00:29:38,731
I called you about our wedding.
You never called back.

370
00:29:38,732 --> 00:29:39,849
No, I didn't.

371
00:29:40,119 --> 00:29:42,823
Hey, friends don't do that.

372
00:29:43,038 --> 00:29:46,241
If they have problems, they talk.
We always did that.

373
00:29:46,416 --> 00:29:49,501
Sometimes good things can
happen from bad ones.

374
00:29:49,711 --> 00:29:52,050
But hey, you're my friend.
So if it'd make you happy...

375
00:29:52,121 --> 00:29:54,343
- I'll divorce her.
- Memo, what are you doing?

376
00:29:54,925 --> 00:29:57,795
Right now, right here, today.
I'm divorced.

377
00:29:58,928 --> 00:30:01,087
But only if you marry me.

378
00:30:01,264 --> 00:30:04,678
- Get out. Come on.
- Please. You know, I get so lonely.

379
00:30:04,693 --> 00:30:07,681
Yeah, you look like you're lonely.

380
00:30:08,687 --> 00:30:12,851
I just want to enjoy my life.
My real life...

381
00:30:13,443 --> 00:30:15,186
not this one.

382
00:30:15,653 --> 00:30:17,147
And Cathy does that for me.

383
00:30:17,863 --> 00:30:22,226
Hey amigo, I have to go. You show these
Maricas what a real driver can do.

384
00:30:22,342 --> 00:30:23,820
- I'll do my best.
- Okay.

385
00:30:24,035 --> 00:30:25,035
Bye.

386
00:30:32,419 --> 00:30:33,617
Sophia!

387
00:30:34,671 --> 00:30:35,916
Where are you going?

388
00:30:37,924 --> 00:30:39,632
Good luck today, Beau.

389
00:30:39,842 --> 00:30:42,844
<i>Everyone excited to see how
Joe Tanto is going to do today.</i>

390
00:30:42,996 --> 00:30:46,014
<i>His first race since
he nearly lost his life.</i>

391
00:30:46,224 --> 00:30:49,924
- Stop bothering people, wise ass.
- Don't mess with me, Tanto.

392
00:30:51,437 --> 00:30:53,830
<i>The force to see...
rookie leader, Jimmy Bly.</i>

393
00:30:53,848 --> 00:30:56,097
<i>It'll be interesting to
see if this young man can</i>

394
00:30:56,109 --> 00:30:58,143
<i>handle the pressure on
this dangerous track.</i>

395
00:30:58,485 --> 00:31:00,485
- What's she doing here?
- It's all right you know.

396
00:31:00,571 --> 00:31:02,091
No, no no, this is very not all right.

397
00:31:02,156 --> 00:31:05,276
Brandenburg's whatever
walks into your life by accident?

398
00:31:05,493 --> 00:31:08,612
- "Whatever"? Hi, I'm Sophia.
- That's your problem.

399
00:31:08,787 --> 00:31:10,281
Demille, come on.

400
00:31:10,956 --> 00:31:14,075
I'm sorry. Weren't you the guy
being pulled in too many directions?

401
00:31:14,669 --> 00:31:15,380
Man.

402
00:31:15,381 --> 00:31:18,311
<i>Well leave now. That'll make
more legroom for the rest of us.</i>

403
00:31:18,346 --> 00:31:22,127
<i>We're at the ready in Toronto.
It's time for the big one to get underway.</i>

404
00:31:22,342 --> 00:31:24,500
Working your way down the track?

405
00:31:25,970 --> 00:31:29,173
<i>Brandenburg is on the pole once again.</i>

406
00:31:29,849 --> 00:31:32,554
<i>As you have heard,
we are ever so close.</i>

407
00:31:46,323 --> 00:31:48,377
<i>We have five minutes to race time.</i>

408
00:31:48,378 --> 00:31:49,378
Joseph.

409
00:31:49,827 --> 00:31:52,033
<i>Gentlemen, to your cars.</i>

410
00:31:58,168 --> 00:32:00,806
Hey, Jimmy. Good luck, man.

411
00:32:01,880 --> 00:32:02,880
Thanks, man.

412
00:32:03,632 --> 00:32:06,221
<i>All the racers you can see
down in pit lane right now...</i>

413
00:32:06,235 --> 00:32:10,084
<i>are in the final stages
of getting ready for this race.</i>

414
00:32:11,181 --> 00:32:13,387
<i>Pace cars are standing by.</i>

415
00:32:16,019 --> 00:32:19,768
<i>We are almost underway
here in Toronto.</i>

416
00:32:22,776 --> 00:32:26,144
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
are you ready for racing?</i>

417
00:32:41,002 --> 00:32:43,124
<i>Gentlemen, start your engines.</i>

418
00:33:08,904 --> 00:33:12,818
<i>Starting today's race from
the pole position, Beau Brandenburg.</i>

419
00:33:13,616 --> 00:33:16,736
<i>Second qualifier, Dario Franchitti.</i>

420
00:33:16,811 --> 00:33:18,787
<i>Third, Christian Fittipaldi.</i>

421
00:33:18,805 --> 00:33:21,340
<i>What they're going to do is
get those tires warmed up to</i>

422
00:33:21,352 --> 00:33:24,033
<i>desired temperature, to get
them tacky for better traction.</i>

423
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:26,921
<i>This is the first
of four warm-up laps.</i>

424
00:33:27,755 --> 00:33:30,791
<i>All eyes on the green flag
ready for it to drop.</i>

425
00:33:31,008 --> 00:33:33,499
<i>Sixteenth, Joe Tanto.</i>

426
00:33:40,601 --> 00:33:41,976
<i>The race is underway!</i>

427
00:33:42,144 --> 00:33:45,429
<i>They roar toward the first turn,
a right-hander, a treacherous gate.</i>

428
00:33:46,064 --> 00:33:48,436
<i>They funnel down into that corner.</i>

429
00:33:57,117 --> 00:33:59,987
<i>Now the second passing
opportunity lies just ahead.</i>

430
00:34:00,203 --> 00:34:03,702
<i>Someone's in trouble!
Two cars sideways, the Visteon car!</i>

431
00:34:03,915 --> 00:34:07,782
<i>Right through the barrier!
He's flipping up end over end!</i>

432
00:34:08,002 --> 00:34:11,038
<i>The Visteon car in big trouble!</i>

433
00:34:16,594 --> 00:34:19,167
<i>An incredible accident!</i>

434
00:34:20,681 --> 00:34:22,508
<i>This puts us at
a full course yellow.</i>

435
00:34:22,724 --> 00:34:26,804
<i>It's gonna give the drivers a chance
for their first pit stops of the day.</i>

436
00:34:28,064 --> 00:34:32,143
<i>One of the strategies to this game
is when to bring your man in.</i>

437
00:34:37,405 --> 00:34:39,997
<i>A single second extra
in the pits can cost a</i>

438
00:34:40,009 --> 00:34:42,612
<i>driver one or two places
in this race today.</i>

439
00:34:53,379 --> 00:34:57,423
<i>There goes Brandenburg.
Bly, and Tanto is out.</i>

440
00:34:57,641 --> 00:35:01,377
<i>All three with very fast pit stops,
just over 12 seconds.</i>

441
00:35:01,554 --> 00:35:06,097
<i>Wow! As Andretti and Tracy almost
get together on the exit!</i>

442
00:35:06,684 --> 00:35:10,467
<i>But now Brandenburg's in front,
Jimmy Bly in second.</i>

443
00:35:11,063 --> 00:35:13,980
I want you to go after Brandenburg.
I want you to go right now. Go!

444
00:35:14,191 --> 00:35:18,319
<i>We have some really interesting driving
by Jimmy Bly behind Brandenburg right now.</i>

445
00:35:18,571 --> 00:35:22,817
- I can't find a hole.
- Don't look for a hole. Make a hole.

446
00:35:23,033 --> 00:35:26,069
<i>Back to full speed,
Bly in pursuit of Brandenburg.</i>

447
00:35:26,202 --> 00:35:29,286
<i>He's right there.
He tries him at every corner.</i>

448
00:35:36,379 --> 00:35:39,131
Jimmy, you got 10 laps to go.
Conserve the tires will you.

449
00:35:39,340 --> 00:35:42,127
You talk into that one more time,
I'm gonna make you eat it.

450
00:35:42,343 --> 00:35:45,048
<i>Don't conserve anything. Go get him.</i>

451
00:35:46,972 --> 00:35:50,757
<i>If he's gonna overtake Brandenburg,
it's gonna happen in Turn 3.</i>

452
00:35:51,019 --> 00:35:52,513
<i>And it's right...</i>

453
00:35:52,728 --> 00:35:55,136
<i>Oh, look at that!</i>

454
00:35:57,358 --> 00:35:58,900
<i>What a way to move!</i>

455
00:35:59,067 --> 00:36:03,231
Jimmy Bly grabs the lead away
from Brandenburg. It's magical.

456
00:36:03,446 --> 00:36:06,069
<i>And Jimmy Bly has just taken the lead!</i>

457
00:36:06,242 --> 00:36:07,784
- Joe.
- Yeah?

458
00:36:07,951 --> 00:36:09,031
I want you to pit now.

459
00:36:09,244 --> 00:36:11,237
Why? I don't need to pit, Carl.

460
00:36:11,621 --> 00:36:13,116
I want you to pit.

461
00:36:13,331 --> 00:36:17,827
<i>In a very unusual move, Carl Henry
has just called Joe Tanto into the pits.</i>

462
00:36:18,086 --> 00:36:20,162
<i>He hit the marks.</i>

463
00:36:20,380 --> 00:36:23,049
I know what you're doing, Carl.
It's wrong.

464
00:36:23,300 --> 00:36:25,588
<i>He's out. They're changing
the tires, they're refueling.</i>

465
00:36:25,802 --> 00:36:29,384
<i>I see no movement on the chassis,
no wing adjustments whatsoever.</i>

466
00:36:29,597 --> 00:36:33,013
I'm not asking you to like this, Joe.
Just work with me.

467
00:36:36,604 --> 00:36:39,973
<i>In the meantime, the veteran
Brandenburg behind Bly.</i>

468
00:36:39,991 --> 00:36:45,315
<i>That's gotta worry the young rookie.
One mistake, that's all it'll take.</i>

469
00:36:45,946 --> 00:36:49,564
- Hold. Hold, Joseph, hold.
- Come on, come on, damn!

470
00:36:54,580 --> 00:36:56,868
Come on, Carl, let me out of here!

471
00:36:58,917 --> 00:37:01,455
<i>Bly in front, Brandenburg second.</i>

472
00:37:01,670 --> 00:37:03,377
Carl, I can't hold him off.

473
00:37:06,841 --> 00:37:09,962
Now, Joe. Go get that son of a bitch.

474
00:37:11,221 --> 00:37:14,305
They release Tanto,
and he roars out of the pit!

475
00:37:14,516 --> 00:37:17,635
<i>I don't know what Carl Henry and his team
were thinking down there at control.</i>

476
00:37:17,852 --> 00:37:21,470
<i>Tanto's making a very fast exit
from the pit. Woah! Look at this!</i>

477
00:37:21,730 --> 00:37:26,393
<i>Tanto slices in between
Bly and Brandenburg!</i>

478
00:37:27,070 --> 00:37:29,643
<i>The officials aren't gonna
like that one.</i>

479
00:37:30,114 --> 00:37:34,443
<i>Tanto has to allow Brandenburg
to pass him after a move like that.</i>

480
00:37:35,994 --> 00:37:37,951
<i>One lap to go now.</i>

481
00:37:41,042 --> 00:37:45,454
<i>It's Bly and Brandenburg battling
it out in the last half-mile.</i>

482
00:37:50,508 --> 00:37:52,750
<i>Brandenburg tries to the inside!</i>

483
00:37:53,803 --> 00:37:57,303
<i>They come off the turn neck and neck.
Who's it gonna be?</i>

484
00:37:58,183 --> 00:38:01,765
<i>And here they come!
The checkered flag is out!</i>

485
00:38:04,689 --> 00:38:07,524
<i>It's Jimmy Bly,
the winner of this race!</i>

486
00:38:08,943 --> 00:38:13,024
<i>As they go around the track,
the checkered flag is flown, and...</i>

487
00:38:13,239 --> 00:38:15,445
Very good strategy, Carl. Thank you.

488
00:38:15,658 --> 00:38:18,742
<i>What a battle between
Jimmy Bly, Beau Brandenburg.</i>

489
00:38:18,953 --> 00:38:22,487
<i>This time, the young rookie
took it to the veteran.</i>

490
00:38:26,418 --> 00:38:28,577
You did all right today, Joseph.

491
00:38:31,715 --> 00:38:33,624
Don't ask me to do that again.

492
00:38:45,646 --> 00:38:50,058
Jimmy, after four lackluster
performances, is Jimmy Bly back?

493
00:38:50,400 --> 00:38:51,598
Well, I hope so.

494
00:38:57,198 --> 00:39:01,066
Everyone falls down.
It's just how fast you get up, right?

495
00:39:02,412 --> 00:39:05,780
Beau, the win could be
called controversial.

496
00:39:06,040 --> 00:39:08,827
- Well, a win is a win.
- So you won't protest?

497
00:39:09,293 --> 00:39:14,085
No, but I will have some lunch.
Anyone wants to join me?

498
00:39:17,051 --> 00:39:18,249
Thank you.

499
00:39:19,261 --> 00:39:21,669
Enjoy. This won't happen again.

500
00:39:43,493 --> 00:39:45,173
Jimmy, want to get together
and talk later?

501
00:39:45,244 --> 00:39:49,492
If he wants to talk, he'll be
talking to me, okay? Come on.

502
00:39:54,212 --> 00:39:56,483
Do you have any idea how much
you'll be worth if you win this title?

503
00:39:56,484 --> 00:39:59,179
Do you even have a clue, they'll be
lining up to buy you in sections.

504
00:39:59,203 --> 00:40:02,175
Everything, your eyes to a sunglass
company, your arm to a watch company.

505
00:40:02,386 --> 00:40:06,384
Or your foot to a shoe company. Or maybe
you'd like to keep some parts for yourself.

506
00:40:06,457 --> 00:40:10,175
- I mean, come on, he just finished racing.
- Hey, you're not here.

507
00:40:10,394 --> 00:40:12,102
- Demille.
- What?

508
00:40:12,546 --> 00:40:14,188
What's so wrong with what she's saying?

509
00:40:15,649 --> 00:40:16,847
Nothing.

510
00:40:19,986 --> 00:40:21,066
Nothing.

511
00:41:20,461 --> 00:41:21,836
What are you doing?

512
00:41:24,215 --> 00:41:25,875
- Swimming.
- Swimming?

513
00:41:26,259 --> 00:41:29,379
That's swimming to you, huh?
I don't think that's swimming.

514
00:41:29,595 --> 00:41:31,303
That's a little beyond.

515
00:41:32,932 --> 00:41:34,474
I've never seen anything like that.

516
00:41:35,184 --> 00:41:38,635
Pretty fantastic.
Where'd you learn how to do that?

517
00:41:42,483 --> 00:41:45,899
- I was raised by frogs.
- Raised by frogs?

518
00:41:53,076 --> 00:41:56,409
- Well, I'm glad you escaped.
- Oh, thank you.

519
00:41:58,081 --> 00:42:00,370
Jimmy, what's on your mind?

520
00:42:04,003 --> 00:42:06,921
- How does Beau do it?
- Do what?

521
00:42:07,548 --> 00:42:10,798
Stay on top. Stay focused.

522
00:42:12,761 --> 00:42:14,304
He drives scared.

523
00:42:15,557 --> 00:42:18,261
No, I don't think so.
That guy is ice.

524
00:42:18,476 --> 00:42:21,809
To you, he's ice. Inside he's scared.

525
00:42:22,980 --> 00:42:26,313
But he likes it.
He says it makes him try harder.

526
00:42:27,818 --> 00:42:30,938
He says the day he's not afraid
is the day he'll stop.

527
00:42:32,072 --> 00:42:34,958
You know you're just as good.
And the day you stop caring...

528
00:42:35,017 --> 00:42:40,030
what other people think and make
yourself happy, you'll be even better.

529
00:42:43,875 --> 00:42:45,038
Come on.

530
00:42:59,265 --> 00:43:01,673
Don't you ever stop running,
cold fish?

531
00:43:01,893 --> 00:43:04,728
Block me again
and I'll put you into the wall.

532
00:43:04,938 --> 00:43:07,226
Now well, that's not gonna happen again.

533
00:43:08,274 --> 00:43:09,436
Believe me.

534
00:43:10,818 --> 00:43:13,439
- What are you trying to prove Joe?
- I got nothing to prove.

535
00:43:13,654 --> 00:43:18,897
No, you proved you could do very
little with very much. Forget it.

536
00:43:19,118 --> 00:43:21,787
Why do I waste my time
talking to this guy?

537
00:43:21,954 --> 00:43:24,789
Because no one else likes
your arrogant ass, that's why.

538
00:43:26,249 --> 00:43:29,369
- So that's it.
- That's it. Mystery solved.

539
00:43:32,005 --> 00:43:35,209
Listen. While you're in this rare good
mood, why don't you do yourself a favor.

540
00:43:35,384 --> 00:43:37,756
- What's that?
- Take her back if she wants you back.

541
00:43:38,011 --> 00:43:41,012
Stay out of my business, Joe.
What are you doing?

542
00:43:41,022 --> 00:43:43,891
I'm just talking. I mean,
you do want her back, right?

543
00:43:44,559 --> 00:43:45,887
Why do you care?

544
00:43:46,018 --> 00:43:49,719
You two have a lot of history.
That doesn't go away so fast.

545
00:43:49,939 --> 00:43:53,225
- I pushed her away, Joe.
- I know, but you weren't thinking right.

546
00:43:53,943 --> 00:43:55,936
I wasn't thinking at all.

547
00:43:57,696 --> 00:44:01,065
You know, it's really hard when...

548
00:44:01,700 --> 00:44:03,278
When I see her with him.

549
00:44:04,369 --> 00:44:06,244
And I did it, you know?

550
00:44:06,706 --> 00:44:09,706
It was me. I'm responsible for it.

551
00:44:11,126 --> 00:44:13,534
You wanted to win no
matter what the cost is.

552
00:44:13,754 --> 00:44:17,253
- You want me to talk to her?
- No, Joe, don't do that.

553
00:44:17,549 --> 00:44:20,218
You don't want to talk to her and
you don't want me to talk to her?

554
00:44:21,929 --> 00:44:23,471
That's just great.

555
00:44:30,019 --> 00:44:33,305
Hey, Beau, if this is about pride,
you better forget it.

556
00:44:33,523 --> 00:44:37,936
- Cause that's how the whole thing started.
- What would you do?

557
00:44:38,111 --> 00:44:41,147
Me? To get someone back
that I really love?

558
00:44:41,364 --> 00:44:43,321
Get that rock out of my stomach?
I'd crawl.

559
00:44:43,533 --> 00:44:45,442
- You'd crawl?
- Crawl.

560
00:44:45,459 --> 00:44:49,573
- Joe. You never crawl.
- I'd crawl till there's nothing left.

561
00:44:50,455 --> 00:44:52,863
Come on, champ. Use your head.

562
00:45:27,226 --> 00:45:29,320
<i>Welcome to ESPN's live coverage...</i>

563
00:45:29,577 --> 00:45:32,578
<i>of the Twin Rings Race of Japan
qualifying section.</i>

564
00:45:32,788 --> 00:45:35,824
<i>And we're live
from the Japan Motor Speedway...</i>

565
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:39,534
<i>in front of 120,000
spectators today.</i>

566
00:45:39,753 --> 00:45:43,454
<i>Open wheel racing,
a very popular sport in Japan.</i>

567
00:45:44,075 --> 00:45:47,709
<i>One day to the event,
and it has been a great day so far.</i>

568
00:45:49,137 --> 00:45:52,200
You should ask Jimmy Bly how it feels to
have the greatest manager in the world.

569
00:45:52,224 --> 00:45:56,268
<i>Yes, with the final run of the day just
completed, the top five best times were.</i>

570
00:45:56,477 --> 00:46:00,939
<i>Brandenburg, Andretti, Gugelmin,
Montoya and Fittipaldi.</i>

571
00:46:01,149 --> 00:46:05,396
<i>An interesting sideline is that this
year's rookie point leader, Jimmy Bly...</i>

572
00:46:05,612 --> 00:46:08,529
<i>only manage a tie
for 10th place.</i>

573
00:46:11,617 --> 00:46:15,912
Relax, dude, don't shove.
Hey, don't shove. We're friends.

574
00:46:16,081 --> 00:46:18,915
Jimmy! Jimmy, why 10th today?

575
00:46:21,752 --> 00:46:24,041
<i>How come this never happens to me?</i>

576
00:46:25,381 --> 00:46:26,381
All right!

577
00:47:05,920 --> 00:47:09,137
- You seem preoccupied during dinner.
- Well, I've been thinking about Jimmy.

578
00:47:09,248 --> 00:47:12,997
You know, Carl thinks he can't cut it.
I think he can. It's just that...

579
00:47:13,218 --> 00:47:16,005
It's tough to get close
to this kid. It is...

580
00:47:16,179 --> 00:47:20,260
I think Carl cares more about helping
you than he does about helping Jimmy.

581
00:47:20,476 --> 00:47:22,255
It looks as if you're
way off on that one.

582
00:47:22,267 --> 00:47:24,058
No, I can tell on the
way he looks at you.

583
00:47:24,271 --> 00:47:28,565
I mean, with Jimmy it's business.
With you... it's personal.

584
00:48:53,523 --> 00:48:58,353
<i>Keep that steady, Jimmy.
Keep your eyes out of the mirror.</i>

585
00:49:04,618 --> 00:49:09,860
<i>With a steady drive, Beau Brandenburg
has managed to catch up to Jimmy Bly.</i>

586
00:49:10,081 --> 00:49:12,637
<i>The veteran Brandenburg
working both sides,</i>

587
00:49:12,649 --> 00:49:15,276
<i>doing everything he can
to make Bly nervous.</i>

588
00:49:15,395 --> 00:49:17,786
<i>Don't let him intimidate you.</i>

589
00:49:21,676 --> 00:49:23,668
I don't know if I can do this.

590
00:49:24,387 --> 00:49:29,382
- You should talk less and drive more.
- Looking great, Jimmy.

591
00:49:30,185 --> 00:49:34,182
<i>Brandenburg knows every inch
of this racetrack.</i>

592
00:49:34,255 --> 00:49:37,521
<i>He moves inside of Bly,
lets him know that he's there.</i>

593
00:49:38,942 --> 00:49:40,436
Let's take him down.

594
00:49:42,112 --> 00:49:45,232
<i>Now it looks like Brandenburg's
gonna try him on the outside.</i>

595
00:49:50,412 --> 00:49:52,120
<i>They're neck and neck!</i>

596
00:49:54,624 --> 00:49:56,996
<i>He gets by!
Brandenburg is now in the lead.</i>

597
00:49:57,210 --> 00:50:00,377
<i>That is some incredible driving
by Beau Brandenburg.</i>

598
00:50:01,798 --> 00:50:03,981
<i>Bly's teammate, Joe Tanto
was instrumental in</i>

599
00:50:03,993 --> 00:50:06,475
<i>getting Bly to the front
of the pack earlier today.</i>

600
00:50:06,653 --> 00:50:09,422
<i>Jimmy, don't let him get to you.
Shake it off.</i>

601
00:50:12,850 --> 00:50:15,852
- I'll get it back. I can get it back.
- Stay on him.

602
00:50:16,062 --> 00:50:19,146
<i>Now we'll see if Bly has learned
through this rookie season.</i>

603
00:50:19,357 --> 00:50:22,274
<i>Can he come back and regain the lead?</i>

604
00:50:24,153 --> 00:50:27,722
<i>- Bly is gonna try it on the high side.
- Don't overdrive the car Jimmy.</i>

605
00:50:28,282 --> 00:50:30,033
Carl, the suspension's
getting loose.

606
00:50:30,045 --> 00:50:32,117
Bly is looking everywhere
on this racetrack.

607
00:50:32,278 --> 00:50:35,329
<i>Inside, outside, high, low,
just nowhere to go.</i>

608
00:50:35,406 --> 00:50:37,663
Damn it! Don't overdrive the car.

609
00:50:37,975 --> 00:50:42,038
<i>The rear is drifting.
Jimmy, keep it steady.</i>

610
00:50:44,798 --> 00:50:46,541
Don't overdrive the car.

611
00:50:53,098 --> 00:50:55,007
Don't overdrive the car.

612
00:50:57,018 --> 00:51:00,268
<i>They're now in the final lap.
This is it. Turn 4. Final turn.</i>

613
00:51:00,438 --> 00:51:05,065
<i>Bly continues to be all over the place.
He's coming up around, he's going high.</i>

614
00:51:05,318 --> 00:51:07,939
<i>Bly's in trouble!
Bly's in serious trouble!</i>

615
00:51:08,154 --> 00:51:12,282
<i>He's off to the gray stuff!
Oh, he slams into the wall!</i>

616
00:51:19,207 --> 00:51:20,998
Oh, my God!

617
00:51:42,979 --> 00:51:45,102
<i>Are you okay, Jimmy?</i>

618
00:51:45,440 --> 00:51:49,519
<i>Safety trucks are rolling.
The crowd on its feet, silent.</i>

619
00:51:57,285 --> 00:52:01,234
<i>We all await word on the fate
of rookie driver Jimmy Bly.</i>

620
00:52:15,844 --> 00:52:19,924
<i>They pull him out from under the car...
and he gives the crowd a wave.</i>

621
00:52:20,140 --> 00:52:24,185
<i>Jimmy Bly, after that
awesome accident, is all right.</i>

622
00:52:24,395 --> 00:52:27,064
<i>And the crowd responds to it.</i>

623
00:52:29,365 --> 00:52:30,388
What a waste.

624
00:52:44,539 --> 00:52:46,244
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, it is
my pleasure to officially</i>

625
00:52:46,256 --> 00:52:48,417
<i>welcome one and all to share
a glimpse of the future...</i>

626
00:52:50,669 --> 00:52:53,989
<i>and the 1000 horsepower magnificent
extreme machines...</i>

627
00:52:54,106 --> 00:52:56,295
<i>that will race us
into the new millennium.</i>

628
00:52:56,467 --> 00:53:00,630
<i>Kindly join me in welcoming
the power and the glory!</i>

629
00:53:10,605 --> 00:53:15,351
Well, Joe. Now what part of formal
didn't you understand?

630
00:53:15,569 --> 00:53:16,979
Well wait a minute.

631
00:53:18,363 --> 00:53:22,491
Oh, my mistake, yeah.
I'm gonna go get a drink.

632
00:53:22,700 --> 00:53:24,574
- You look very nice.
- Thank you.

633
00:53:24,785 --> 00:53:26,529
- Hey, rebel.
- Yeah.

634
00:53:26,746 --> 00:53:27,909
Well what you got there?

635
00:53:28,081 --> 00:53:30,750
Oh it's a little something I want
to give to Jimmy later on.

636
00:53:31,167 --> 00:53:33,758
Top of your hands, be selective
who you spend time with.

637
00:53:33,836 --> 00:53:36,920
Extend yourself. These are people
who make everything happen.

638
00:53:37,131 --> 00:53:39,800
- He's right.
- You'll stay around, right?

639
00:53:39,925 --> 00:53:41,336
I'll be around.

640
00:53:42,678 --> 00:53:44,885
You do know your way around,
don't you?

641
00:53:45,097 --> 00:53:48,217
- I like your brother.
- I liked him first.

642
00:53:48,434 --> 00:53:52,217
- Demille?
- Nina. Exactly who I wanted to see.

643
00:53:52,563 --> 00:53:55,647
- You look fantastic.
- Thank you.

644
00:53:55,941 --> 00:54:01,018
Earlier today you said that Jimmy
has to find it off the track.

645
00:54:01,447 --> 00:54:04,364
- What did you mean by that?
- Here we go with the questions.

646
00:54:04,991 --> 00:54:06,189
Gotta find that quiet spot.

647
00:54:06,409 --> 00:54:10,110
If the race in your mind's not right,
you will get torn apart.

648
00:54:10,622 --> 00:54:14,535
So you better buckle up.
It's gonna be a bumpy ride.

649
00:54:16,127 --> 00:54:19,247
I can't believe that line still works.

650
00:54:21,549 --> 00:54:25,381
Now this is either very
unprofessional, or naive...

651
00:54:25,636 --> 00:54:29,005
or she swallowed all your bullshit
and loved the taste.

652
00:54:29,223 --> 00:54:33,055
- Where's Memo?
- Replacing you. Working his way down.

653
00:54:33,311 --> 00:54:37,557
Joe, if you don't get it by midnight,
you're probably not gonna get it.

654
00:54:38,232 --> 00:54:41,316
And even if you do,
I don't think it's gonna be worth it.

655
00:54:43,403 --> 00:54:45,194
Just an observation.

656
00:54:55,790 --> 00:54:57,035
Excuse me.

657
00:54:58,042 --> 00:54:59,536
Did you make any new friends?

658
00:54:59,752 --> 00:55:03,667
Like these people want to talk to me.
Listen, when the season's over...

659
00:55:03,840 --> 00:55:06,509
- What?
- I was thinking...

660
00:55:06,676 --> 00:55:10,259
maybe we could go someplace.
I've never even had a vacation.

661
00:55:11,305 --> 00:55:13,298
- Never?
- Never.

662
00:55:15,392 --> 00:55:18,263
But hey. No pressure, all right?
Just think about it.

663
00:55:19,521 --> 00:55:21,361
Jimmy please. Just two
minutes, come on please?

664
00:55:25,819 --> 00:55:27,611
What a coincidence.

665
00:55:30,866 --> 00:55:33,985
Is this a little experiment
for you or something?

666
00:55:34,411 --> 00:55:37,282
Dark chapter you can tell
your friends about?

667
00:55:38,665 --> 00:55:41,203
Maybe you like being manhandled.

668
00:55:41,793 --> 00:55:43,371
That I can understand. But...

669
00:55:43,586 --> 00:55:46,955
it's the being dumped part
that's kind of a drag.

670
00:55:48,841 --> 00:55:51,878
So you were just used and abused?

671
00:55:52,596 --> 00:55:54,588
Was that attitude?

672
00:55:55,890 --> 00:55:58,179
Saucy. Good for you.

673
00:56:01,771 --> 00:56:05,602
And next time I'm around, look at him.
He ain't over it.

674
00:56:07,567 --> 00:56:09,395
Your mascara's running.

675
00:56:12,823 --> 00:56:14,365
That's cute.

676
00:56:16,535 --> 00:56:18,326
Stupid bitch.

677
00:56:18,662 --> 00:56:22,659
- So, are you two enjoying the evening?
- I'll wait over there.

678
00:56:22,874 --> 00:56:26,125
Ok quickly. If you win a championship,
what'd be the first that you'd do?

679
00:56:26,670 --> 00:56:28,438
I don't know, really.

680
00:56:28,439 --> 00:56:29,696
Well, I'd throw a party.

681
00:56:29,731 --> 00:56:32,012
Anyway, you've had some peaks
and valleys over the season.

682
00:56:32,217 --> 00:56:34,297
What have you learned that
you never realized before?

683
00:56:34,427 --> 00:56:37,593
Jimmy, what have you learned
that you never realized before?

684
00:56:37,763 --> 00:56:40,638
- Boy, that it's another world out there.
- Where air is rare.

685
00:56:40,759 --> 00:56:43,844
Now your team has positioned to take it all
with a strong show in Germany.

686
00:56:44,062 --> 00:56:46,469
Tell us how do you prepare
for something like...?

687
00:56:46,689 --> 00:56:49,514
<i>Well there you have it, ladies and gentlemen.
You know James.</i>

688
00:56:49,526 --> 00:56:52,027
<i>Bly obviously very pensive
about the upcoming race.</i>

689
00:56:52,278 --> 00:56:54,069
- Yeah, well...
- What's happening?

690
00:56:54,655 --> 00:56:56,944
- What's does it look like?
- Jimmy.

691
00:56:57,158 --> 00:57:00,194
- You came here with me.
- I think maybe gonna leave with you...

692
00:57:00,411 --> 00:57:03,246
but what I have to say to her
you don't need to hear, ok?

693
00:57:03,414 --> 00:57:06,663
Just let him talk.
It doesn't mean anything.

694
00:57:06,833 --> 00:57:10,831
- Yes, it does mean something.
- What, Beau? What does it mean?

695
00:57:12,631 --> 00:57:15,169
Ok, we should probably just go.
Come on, Sophia, let's go.

696
00:57:15,384 --> 00:57:17,590
- Hey, don't do that.
- Don't do what?

697
00:57:17,803 --> 00:57:21,302
- That's none of your business, ok.
- Guys guys, come on. What's going on?

698
00:57:21,514 --> 00:57:24,052
- It's nothing, Demille.
- Back off.

699
00:57:27,061 --> 00:57:29,683
Jimmy. Come with me for a second.
Can I talk to you?

700
00:57:29,898 --> 00:57:32,898
- You're doing this all wrong.
- I know.

701
00:57:33,526 --> 00:57:35,068
I do everything wrong.

702
00:57:35,319 --> 00:57:38,190
- Excuse us.
- I can't believe this is happening.

703
00:57:39,865 --> 00:57:42,736
I just don't want to spend
more time away from you. I...

704
00:57:44,203 --> 00:57:45,828
I miss you.

705
00:57:48,290 --> 00:57:49,701
I miss you too.

706
00:57:51,543 --> 00:57:54,461
- Really?
- Yeah.

707
00:57:54,880 --> 00:58:00,170
Do not go over there. Trust me.
Jimmy, please. Calm down, calm down.

708
00:58:00,386 --> 00:58:04,928
Jimmy. Don't blow this. Not over her.
This is not eighth-grade prom.

709
00:58:05,140 --> 00:58:07,631
How you act,
these things are important.

710
00:58:08,059 --> 00:58:10,218
- Jesus Christ!
- He's giving her a ring.

711
00:58:10,436 --> 00:58:12,595
- Obviously not good.
- Please take it back.

712
00:58:12,855 --> 00:58:17,317
Whatever it is, you can deal
with it later. This is not the time.

713
00:58:18,194 --> 00:58:20,021
Just work with me on this.

714
00:58:20,280 --> 00:58:21,525
Jimmy.

715
00:58:25,409 --> 00:58:27,034
I'm so sorry.

716
00:58:28,078 --> 00:58:30,747
Go. Just go.

717
00:58:32,792 --> 00:58:33,990
I don't...

718
00:58:34,794 --> 00:58:36,870
- Just let me explain it to you.
- Hey, you need...

719
00:58:38,380 --> 00:58:39,380
Get away from me.

720
00:58:39,465 --> 00:58:41,909
- Go play your game somewhere else.
- Sophia just listen to me.

721
00:58:41,933 --> 00:58:43,658
- Five minutes.
- Go away!

722
00:58:43,768 --> 00:58:45,425
- Jimmy.
- Don't push me, don't push me.

723
00:58:45,595 --> 00:58:47,619
- Go.
- Fine, fine, okay!

724
00:58:47,654 --> 00:58:50,054
- Play your game somewhere else.
- Get the hell away from me.

725
00:59:06,575 --> 00:59:08,318
Move, move, move! Move!

726
01:00:35,118 --> 01:00:36,149
I need backup!

727
01:00:39,956 --> 01:00:40,956
Pull over!

728
01:00:41,500 --> 01:00:43,077
Come on, Jimmy, pull over!

729
01:02:23,640 --> 01:02:25,383
Get away from me, man. Just...

730
01:02:25,600 --> 01:02:27,327
What? You want to go through me?
Come on. Go through me.

731
01:02:27,351 --> 01:02:28,945
I don't want to fight you.
I want to fight him.

732
01:02:28,969 --> 01:02:30,142
- For what?
- For what?

733
01:02:30,177 --> 01:02:30,979
You weren't there?

734
01:02:31,188 --> 01:02:32,471
I was there. What do
you think he did, take

735
01:02:32,483 --> 01:02:33,951
your woman away? Is that
what you think he did?

736
01:02:33,975 --> 01:02:35,369
Why did I let him just take her away?

737
01:02:35,393 --> 01:02:37,586
She was gone, Jimmy.
She was always gonna leave. You know it.

738
01:02:37,603 --> 01:02:39,381
You don't know that you're talking about.
What do you know bout it anyway?

739
01:02:39,405 --> 01:02:41,716
I know that your brother puts so much
pressure on you to win...

740
01:02:41,740 --> 01:02:44,248
that you looking for an edge.
And you figured... she was it.

741
01:02:44,268 --> 01:02:46,148
Why do you act like you
even care about me, Joe?

742
01:02:46,244 --> 01:02:48,244
I'm just a thing to you,
just part of the job, huh?

743
01:02:48,413 --> 01:02:50,242
You pick up a paycheck to
help me out because you

744
01:02:50,254 --> 01:02:52,015
didn't help yourself
when you had the chance.

745
01:02:52,334 --> 01:02:54,103
Why does that make you better
you so much better than me Joe?

746
01:02:54,127 --> 01:02:56,038
It doesn't, Bly.
You take the car because of him?

747
01:02:56,062 --> 01:02:57,481
I don't need anyone else pushing on me.

748
01:02:57,505 --> 01:02:59,165
- Go on, say it.
- Forget this.

749
01:02:59,382 --> 01:03:01,292
Totally out of control. What
you did tonight would get

750
01:03:01,304 --> 01:03:03,487
you thrown out because you've
been looking for the exit.

751
01:03:03,511 --> 01:03:05,238
And you don't even know what
the hell you're talking about?

752
01:03:05,262 --> 01:03:07,505
And you don't know who you are anymore!

753
01:03:07,807 --> 01:03:09,437
So you're putting in
your mind you've got to

754
01:03:09,449 --> 01:03:11,209
be perfect every time out
or you're a failure.

755
01:03:11,244 --> 01:03:14,310
Well, forget that. Just forget it.

756
01:03:25,992 --> 01:03:28,909
I was gonna give this to you
before all this went down tonight.

757
01:03:29,370 --> 01:03:30,745
Impressive, isn't it?

758
01:03:34,541 --> 01:03:37,459
- What is it?
- It's the first thing I ever won.

759
01:03:37,670 --> 01:03:40,789
When I won it was probably the last time
I ever felt pure victory.

760
01:03:41,006 --> 01:03:43,979
No pressure, nobody breathing
down my back.

761
01:03:44,059 --> 01:03:45,751
Just driving because I loved it.
Pure.

762
01:03:45,969 --> 01:03:49,587
That's where you've gotta get back to.
Doing what you do naturally, just for you.

763
01:03:49,764 --> 01:03:53,049
I mean I don't have your gift, but I do
have a couple of things you don't have.

764
01:03:53,225 --> 01:03:56,595
I got will and I got faith.
Wait, don't laugh, I'm serious.

765
01:03:57,564 --> 01:04:01,182
Because I believe that you can will yourself
into anything and do anything.

766
01:04:01,984 --> 01:04:04,024
Have faith, that's like
believing in something...

767
01:04:04,695 --> 01:04:07,364
Man, that's like having a good disease,
it's contagious.

768
01:04:07,573 --> 01:04:10,693
If you hang around with people that
have it, you're gonna catch it.

769
01:04:10,910 --> 01:04:12,949
That's gonna change your attitude.

770
01:04:13,371 --> 01:04:15,493
And winning is an attitude.

771
01:04:16,207 --> 01:04:18,282
So if you trust me...
No, if you trust yourself...

772
01:04:18,500 --> 01:04:21,536
by this end of the season,
you'll either be on top or you won't.

773
01:04:21,712 --> 01:04:25,543
But I guarantee you're gonna know
what Jimmy Bly is really made of.

774
01:04:39,437 --> 01:04:41,560
<i>Outside Chicago,
at the chicane it goes up...</i>

775
01:04:41,815 --> 01:04:44,566
<i>and comes down right where you
got Brandenburg...</i>

776
01:04:44,776 --> 01:04:46,270
Is that when I dip down?

777
01:04:47,820 --> 01:04:49,149
Forget it.

778
01:04:49,614 --> 01:04:52,614
I'm tired of these spoons.
We play with spoons.

779
01:04:52,825 --> 01:04:55,031
- Say "ah."
- Ah.

780
01:04:55,202 --> 01:04:56,945
<i>Welcome to Germany.
Home of beer...</i>

781
01:04:58,289 --> 01:05:00,412
<i>the Autobahn and Beau Brandenburg.</i>

782
01:05:01,751 --> 01:05:03,155
<i>Qualifying begins tomorrow.</i>

783
01:05:03,156 --> 01:05:05,884
<i>With just two races
remaining in the season...</i>

784
01:05:05,919 --> 01:05:08,559
<i>Beau Brandenburg is leading in the race
for the world championship.</i>

785
01:05:09,174 --> 01:05:10,633
<i>Jimmy Bly is in second.</i>

786
01:05:10,842 --> 01:05:13,163
We just learned that
Racing Commissioner Nathan.

787
01:05:13,175 --> 01:05:15,556
Gilson has slapped Bly and
teammate, Joe Tanto...

788
01:05:15,672 --> 01:05:17,979
<i>with a $ 25,000 fine...</i>

789
01:05:18,091 --> 01:05:21,141
<i>for their recent joyride
through downtown Chicago.</i>

790
01:05:34,991 --> 01:05:37,482
<i>Doing great, Jimmy.
Keep pushing that speed.</i>

791
01:05:41,872 --> 01:05:42,903
Hey.

792
01:05:43,249 --> 01:05:45,040
You don't need to talk to me anymore?

793
01:05:45,250 --> 01:05:48,287
- It's not like that.
- Really? What is it like?

794
01:05:49,964 --> 01:05:52,537
All right, here you go. Jimmy.

795
01:06:36,843 --> 01:06:38,243
<i>Three, two.</i>

796
01:06:38,335 --> 01:06:39,879
<i>One. Beautiful. Come on, buddy.</i>

797
01:06:42,181 --> 01:06:45,347
Now, is he a hero, or is it hype?
What do you think?

798
01:06:45,892 --> 01:06:47,495
I don't know Carl. What
do you want me to say?

799
01:06:47,519 --> 01:06:48,904
I want to hear what you think!

800
01:06:48,928 --> 01:06:51,816
Jimmy just needs time
to develop, that's all. It's a little time.

801
01:06:51,932 --> 01:06:55,086
But I think when he can get it together off
the track, he will come together on.

802
01:06:55,110 --> 01:06:56,688
That's what I think.

803
01:06:57,487 --> 01:06:58,602
Like you got it together?

804
01:06:59,406 --> 01:07:03,038
I've decided you can help the kid off
the track more than on it.

805
01:07:03,073 --> 01:07:06,530
You're not gonna be racing on Sunday.
I'm gonna bringing Memo back.

806
01:07:07,682 --> 01:07:10,140
Come here. Joseph, over here.

807
01:07:11,527 --> 01:07:12,606
Sit.

808
01:07:13,237 --> 01:07:14,237
At my level.

809
01:07:16,281 --> 01:07:18,238
It's the moment of truth, my friend.

810
01:07:19,367 --> 01:07:22,452
If he doesn't deliver
next time out, he goes.

811
01:07:24,665 --> 01:07:27,288
Don't hate me, Joe.
But you go with him.

812
01:07:28,126 --> 01:07:30,035
I'm gonna come around here in Turn 7.

813
01:07:30,654 --> 01:07:33,375
I'm gonna driving off Brandenburg,
I'm gonna fake outside.

814
01:07:33,590 --> 01:07:35,249
And eight's a tough place to pass.

815
01:07:35,425 --> 01:07:37,277
I'm gonna carry that speed inside...

816
01:07:37,312 --> 01:07:40,129
bring it down back on the straightaway.
We'd have plenty of speed.

817
01:07:40,347 --> 01:07:41,426
Kind of flawless.

818
01:07:41,598 --> 01:07:44,219
You're not even paying attention.
Watch this.

819
01:07:44,434 --> 01:07:46,177
Show me again.

820
01:08:01,992 --> 01:08:03,026
Yes, sir.

821
01:08:03,027 --> 01:08:07,620
If you find yourself in a position
to hold up traffic, do it.

822
01:08:07,981 --> 01:08:09,789
I don't want any front-running.

823
01:08:10,543 --> 01:08:12,120
You know the drill.

824
01:08:19,676 --> 01:08:22,926
- Don't hurt yourself.
- I just told you and I told you too.

825
01:08:25,431 --> 01:08:27,410
- What does that mean?
- I told you that I'll return.

826
01:08:27,434 --> 01:08:29,142
Here I am, returned.

827
01:08:29,769 --> 01:08:31,643
Like the real Zorro.

828
01:08:32,105 --> 01:08:34,892
There's no helmet big enough
to hold that head.

829
01:08:35,107 --> 01:08:36,685
There's so much love in here.

830
01:08:36,859 --> 01:08:38,935
You keep smiling,
your face is gonna crack.

831
01:08:41,447 --> 01:08:44,781
Why shouldn't he smile?
He's got a lot to be happy about.

832
01:08:44,992 --> 01:08:46,901
He's back where he belongs.
Right, baby?

833
01:08:47,411 --> 01:08:48,490
Yep.

834
01:08:49,830 --> 01:08:51,028
Good?

835
01:08:51,290 --> 01:08:52,832
Hey, you're so good.

836
01:08:53,083 --> 01:08:55,040
You win this, yeah?

837
01:08:55,293 --> 01:08:56,918
You're gonna win.

838
01:08:58,129 --> 01:09:00,751
- Be safe, all right?
- You too, be safe.

839
01:09:22,665 --> 01:09:24,231
<i>We're at the German Motor Speedway.</i>

840
01:09:24,266 --> 01:09:27,510
<i>This is the second to last race
of the season.</i>

841
01:09:27,545 --> 01:09:29,944
<i>And what an exciting one
it promises to be.</i>

842
01:09:34,665 --> 01:09:36,025
<i>The clouds are all around here...</i>

843
01:09:36,092 --> 01:09:39,992
<i>and it looks like there's a thunderstorm
maybe a mile or two from the track.</i>

844
01:09:40,170 --> 01:09:41,879
<i>The threat of rain hasn't dampened...</i>

845
01:09:41,955 --> 01:09:45,292
<i>the spirits of this capacity crowd
here in Germany.</i>

846
01:09:51,140 --> 01:09:52,140
What do you want?

847
01:09:54,267 --> 01:09:55,430
I wanted to apologize.

848
01:09:56,311 --> 01:09:58,350
Apologize to yourself.

849
01:09:59,147 --> 01:10:00,557
Let's race.

850
01:10:12,785 --> 01:10:15,454
I want you to stay in your world
and don't get into his.

851
01:10:15,621 --> 01:10:18,159
You push him hard.
You get him thinking about you.

852
01:10:19,334 --> 01:10:21,243
And you're not thinking about him.

853
01:10:21,461 --> 01:10:22,461
Got it.

854
01:10:34,014 --> 01:10:38,142
<i>The skies are opening up
as the warm-up lap begins.</i>

855
01:10:51,031 --> 01:10:52,193
How's Jimmy?

856
01:10:52,365 --> 01:10:53,397
He's all there.

857
01:11:08,715 --> 01:11:11,040
<i>We are racing in Germany.</i>

858
01:11:11,259 --> 01:11:14,674
<i>Beau Brandenburg is starting
in the pole position today.</i>

859
01:11:22,477 --> 01:11:24,767
<i>Jimmy Bly is in second.</i>

860
01:11:25,189 --> 01:11:29,386
<i>Brandenburg moves out in front
on a road course you can race in the rain.</i>

861
01:11:29,643 --> 01:11:32,977
<i>Rain tires are on
and they are at speed.</i>

862
01:11:35,782 --> 01:11:39,401
<i>Memo Moreno is back, giving
Jimmy Bly a little help as his teammate.</i>

863
01:11:39,619 --> 01:11:42,656
<i>I'm sure Memo wants to make
his presence felt here today.</i>

864
01:11:43,957 --> 01:11:45,632
<i>Boy, he is on the fly.</i>

865
01:11:45,742 --> 01:11:47,700
<i>It's like he has something to prove.</i>

866
01:11:48,085 --> 01:11:49,085
Good move, Memo.

867
01:11:50,238 --> 01:11:51,915
<i>Keep it steady.</i>

868
01:11:52,715 --> 01:11:55,206
Somebody wants their job back.

869
01:11:55,426 --> 01:11:59,376
<i>I think Joe Tanto may want
to watch his back.</i>

870
01:12:04,226 --> 01:12:05,601
<i>Oops, somebody's spinning!</i>

871
01:12:05,811 --> 01:12:07,521
<i>Kenny Brack, he's in trouble.</i>

872
01:12:07,596 --> 01:12:10,017
<i>He's gonna go way back
in the field on that one.</i>

873
01:12:10,273 --> 01:12:12,682
<i>Back at the front
the battle continues.</i>

874
01:12:15,737 --> 01:12:18,359
<i>Look at Brandenburg.
He cuts off Bly!</i>

875
01:12:18,615 --> 01:12:19,580
He tried to take me out.

876
01:12:19,592 --> 01:12:21,584
Jimmy, you got to detach it.
Just hold your line.

877
01:12:21,718 --> 01:12:23,491
<i>Ride his blind spot.</i>

878
01:12:25,413 --> 01:12:28,035
I will, Joe,
but I can't see a damn thing.

879
01:12:28,250 --> 01:12:31,085
<i>Neither can he.
Just patience, my man. Patience.</i>

880
01:12:52,981 --> 01:12:54,061
Take him, Jimmy! Take him!

881
01:12:55,525 --> 01:12:57,103
<i>Jimmy Bly in second place.</i>

882
01:12:57,277 --> 01:12:59,567
<i>Putting the pressure
on Beau Brandenburg.</i>

883
01:13:03,992 --> 01:13:04,992
Push it.

884
01:13:07,621 --> 01:13:08,783
Here we go.

885
01:13:11,499 --> 01:13:14,134
<i>Jimmy Bly is gonna try to make
a move in the corner...</i>

886
01:13:14,144 --> 01:13:17,000
<i>on Brandenburg on the outside.
And he does it!</i>

887
01:13:17,114 --> 01:13:18,957
<i>Bly takes the lead.</i>

888
01:13:20,258 --> 01:13:21,669
Goddamn brilliant.

889
01:13:22,827 --> 01:13:25,500
<i>There's a car in trouble, spinning
on the wet pavement.</i>

890
01:13:25,680 --> 01:13:28,597
<i>- That looks like Gidley.
- Oh, here comes Max Papis!</i>

891
01:13:29,391 --> 01:13:30,767
<i>Crash!</i>

892
01:13:31,978 --> 01:13:36,106
<i>Head-on into that car!
Max Papis is airborne.</i>

893
01:13:45,449 --> 01:13:47,693
If he takes it to the
inside, it drops down.

894
01:13:47,705 --> 01:13:49,661
Don't follow him,
he's setting you up.

895
01:13:50,287 --> 01:13:52,743
<i>In the hairpin, that fight
for the lead continues.</i>

896
01:13:52,956 --> 01:13:54,534
<i>Jimmy Bly has the lead now.</i>

897
01:13:54,750 --> 01:13:57,240
<i>Brandenburg wants it back.</i>

898
01:14:00,672 --> 01:14:03,458
<i>Brandenburg goes to the high side.</i>

899
01:14:03,842 --> 01:14:05,301
<i>He gets by!</i>

900
01:14:05,510 --> 01:14:07,581
<i>Brandenburg back to the lead.</i>

901
01:14:08,596 --> 01:14:10,304
Just keep cool, he's putting on a show.

902
01:14:10,598 --> 01:14:11,598
It's a hell of a show.

903
01:14:12,809 --> 01:14:14,053
Yeah, hell of a show.

904
01:14:14,685 --> 01:14:18,385
<i>Now Memo Moreno whips out
of the pack and passes Andretti.</i>

905
01:14:18,564 --> 01:14:22,147
<i>He's really trying to get up there
with Brandenburg and Bly.</i>

906
01:14:22,360 --> 01:14:23,474
<i>Memo, what are you doing?</i>

907
01:14:23,736 --> 01:14:25,064
<i>I can almost touch him.</i>

908
01:14:25,279 --> 01:14:26,821
Hold your position.

909
01:14:27,031 --> 01:14:28,062
Why? He's can win this.

910
01:14:28,907 --> 01:14:32,110
<i>I'm sure Carl Henry is not
too happy with Moreno.</i>

911
01:14:32,494 --> 01:14:34,901
<i>Now Bly wants to make a move.</i>

912
01:14:35,163 --> 01:14:37,503
<i>Hold on, Memo Moreno
trying to make...</i>

913
01:14:37,616 --> 01:14:40,417
<i>the same move on Jimmy Bly,
his teammate.</i>

914
01:14:40,586 --> 01:14:43,123
Memo, no passing.
Do you hear me?

915
01:14:43,547 --> 01:14:44,661
But I'm right there, Carl.

916
01:14:46,257 --> 01:14:48,754
Memo, lift off. Keep it steady.
What the hell are you doing?

917
01:14:48,885 --> 01:14:51,506
<i>Moreno appears to have something
to prove here.</i>

918
01:14:51,762 --> 01:14:53,590
<i>He gets alongside Bly again.</i>

919
01:14:53,849 --> 01:14:55,129
Damn it Memo, we went over this!

920
01:14:55,600 --> 01:14:56,600
Lift off!

921
01:14:58,311 --> 01:15:00,434
Lift off! You work for me.
I said, lift off.

922
01:15:00,605 --> 01:15:03,027
Why the hell don't you let him drive?
Come on, baby.

923
01:15:03,140 --> 01:15:05,063
- Come on. Come on. Come on!
- Shut up!

924
01:15:08,488 --> 01:15:09,519
I've got to do this.

925
01:15:09,739 --> 01:15:12,574
<i>With his teammate in the middle of
the battle for the championship...</i>

926
01:15:12,783 --> 01:15:15,784
<i>Moreno has decided to stick
his nose into this fight.</i>

927
01:15:15,995 --> 01:15:17,074
Hey, Memo, back off.

928
01:15:17,246 --> 01:15:19,618
<i>Only inches separate
these two cars.</i>

929
01:15:19,873 --> 01:15:21,073
Memo, you're too close.

930
01:16:10,755 --> 01:16:13,045
<i>What's going on here?
Bly is spinning.</i>

931
01:16:13,634 --> 01:16:17,216
<i>He gets it under control.
He's going backwards on the track.</i>

932
01:16:17,679 --> 01:16:18,842
Jimmy, what are you doing?

933
01:16:20,390 --> 01:16:22,133
Jimmy, what the hell are you doing?

934
01:16:41,994 --> 01:16:43,156
Memo?

935
01:16:58,718 --> 01:17:00,546
Get out! Oh, God!

936
01:17:01,931 --> 01:17:03,651
<i>We're getting pictures
now from the chopper.</i>

937
01:17:03,849 --> 01:17:08,012
<i>This is horrible.
The car is upside down.</i>

938
01:17:08,228 --> 01:17:11,679
<i>It's in a body of water of some sort.
Moreno is pinned underwater.</i>

939
01:17:17,279 --> 01:17:18,903
It's okay, Memo. I'm here.

940
01:17:19,114 --> 01:17:22,529
<i>Beau, Memo crashed badly.
Jimmy went after him. You've gotta go help.</i>

941
01:17:22,742 --> 01:17:24,467
He went into the river at Turn 5.

942
01:17:24,677 --> 01:17:27,447
I'll get you out, Memo.
It's gonna be okay.

943
01:17:30,883 --> 01:17:33,575
- I'm on my way.
- Beau, what are you gonna do?

944
01:17:33,795 --> 01:17:35,170
<i>Please be careful.</i>

945
01:17:36,839 --> 01:17:38,417
Oh, God! My foot!

946
01:17:39,967 --> 01:17:41,378
Oh, come on.

947
01:17:42,136 --> 01:17:44,709
<i>Hang on, Memo! Hang on!</i>

948
01:17:45,180 --> 01:17:46,888
- Help me!
- Get out!

949
01:17:47,557 --> 01:17:50,475
- Help me!
- Get out, now!

950
01:17:50,978 --> 01:17:52,686
It's gonna blow up!

951
01:17:54,690 --> 01:17:55,852
Hurry!

952
01:18:02,030 --> 01:18:05,565
<i>We've got Bly and Brandenburg
to help a man in trouble.</i>

953
01:18:06,076 --> 01:18:09,112
<i>Rescue teams are on the way,
but the remote location...</i>

954
01:18:09,287 --> 01:18:11,956
<i>of this crash is making
it difficult to reach them.</i>

955
01:18:12,415 --> 01:18:15,451
Lift it up, higher. Lift it!

956
01:18:20,005 --> 01:18:22,960
Take a breath, Memo.
Come on. We're here.

957
01:18:23,676 --> 01:18:25,004
We're gonna get you out.

958
01:18:26,887 --> 01:18:28,381
Now!

959
01:18:28,764 --> 01:18:30,175
Come on. One, two...

960
01:18:32,851 --> 01:18:35,093
Get it over. Memo!

961
01:18:35,562 --> 01:18:36,974
We got you.

962
01:18:38,566 --> 01:18:40,641
- Come on, Memo.
- I can't move my leg!

963
01:18:41,318 --> 01:18:42,318
Come on.

964
01:18:42,569 --> 01:18:43,814
It's gonna be okay.

965
01:18:43,929 --> 01:18:45,029
<i>Gotta be fuel everywhere.</i>

966
01:18:45,180 --> 01:18:47,161
<i>Well if that's the case, they
better get that driver out</i>

967
01:18:47,173 --> 01:18:49,226
<i>of there and they better get
themselves out of there...</i>

968
01:18:49,250 --> 01:18:53,079
<i>because that fuel could ignite,
it could be floating on top of the water.</i>

969
01:18:57,125 --> 01:18:58,500
Come on!

970
01:19:00,378 --> 01:19:01,540
Hurry up!

971
01:19:26,053 --> 01:19:28,027
<i>That is horrifying.</i>

972
01:19:28,197 --> 01:19:30,117
<i>I don't think I've never
seen anything like that.</i>

973
01:19:30,199 --> 01:19:32,405
<i>It's unbelievable.</i>

974
01:19:32,784 --> 01:19:36,616
<i>Worried about the well-being
of another driver, another competitor.</i>

975
01:19:37,455 --> 01:19:41,039
<i>Just goes to show the kind of men
that they are, their true fabric.</i>

976
01:19:41,251 --> 01:19:44,086
<i>But they worked as a team together.</i>

977
01:19:47,382 --> 01:19:50,386
<i>Oh, my God, look at that!
Are they okay?</i>

978
01:19:50,401 --> 01:19:52,294
<i>It looks like they are.
I think I see...</i>

979
01:19:52,470 --> 01:19:53,845
<i>I see movement.</i>

980
01:20:08,068 --> 01:20:11,852
I can't move my legs.
I can't move them.

981
01:20:20,038 --> 01:20:21,367
Jimmy?

982
01:20:21,540 --> 01:20:22,950
Jimmy? You all right?

983
01:20:23,166 --> 01:20:23,996
Yes, just my foot.

984
01:20:24,167 --> 01:20:26,840
You'll be fine, ok.
You'll come through this just fine.

985
01:20:27,020 --> 01:20:29,180
- How's Memo?
- Memo's fine, they're looking after him.

986
01:20:42,309 --> 01:20:47,304
<i>Our thoughts, of course, with Memo
Moreno and his family at this point.</i>

987
01:20:57,449 --> 01:20:58,943
Hey, Memo.

988
01:20:59,409 --> 01:21:00,488
Hey, Joe.

989
01:21:02,538 --> 01:21:03,569
How do I look?

990
01:21:04,873 --> 01:21:05,873
Never looked better.

991
01:21:09,044 --> 01:21:11,416
- Jimmy?
- Yeah?

992
01:21:12,088 --> 01:21:13,088
Hey.

993
01:21:14,174 --> 01:21:15,716
Thanks.

994
01:21:16,300 --> 01:21:18,839
- Memo, I'm sorry.
- You came back for me.

995
01:21:19,262 --> 01:21:21,089
Saved my life.

996
01:21:21,765 --> 01:21:22,879
We race.

997
01:21:23,600 --> 01:21:25,509
We take chances.

998
01:21:26,561 --> 01:21:27,806
I took this chance.

999
01:21:28,771 --> 01:21:30,265
So look at me, huh.

1000
01:21:31,982 --> 01:21:33,358
Look at me.

1001
01:21:33,526 --> 01:21:35,020
Don't see you.

1002
01:21:36,404 --> 01:21:37,779
See me.

1003
01:21:39,390 --> 01:21:41,482
The one who made a mistake.

1004
01:21:43,827 --> 01:21:45,072
That's all.

1005
01:21:46,705 --> 01:21:48,164
It wasn't a mistake.

1006
01:22:18,027 --> 01:22:19,521
How are you doing?

1007
01:22:20,946 --> 01:22:22,275
I'm all right.

1008
01:22:22,532 --> 01:22:24,608
All right if I come in?

1009
01:22:25,493 --> 01:22:26,691
Yeah.

1010
01:22:30,789 --> 01:22:32,165
You tried to get him out.

1011
01:22:32,875 --> 01:22:33,875
So did you.

1012
01:22:34,084 --> 01:22:35,163
You were there first.

1013
01:22:36,169 --> 01:22:39,337
I mean, he almost got you killed
and you still tried.

1014
01:22:39,965 --> 01:22:40,965
Anybody would've.

1015
01:22:41,800 --> 01:22:43,045
Would they?

1016
01:22:45,637 --> 01:22:47,179
You're a good man, Jimmy.

1017
01:22:47,389 --> 01:22:51,433
I'm sorry, I didn't want to win
the championship this way.

1018
01:22:52,518 --> 01:22:53,518
See you.

1019
01:23:29,305 --> 01:23:33,598
You know, the old Joe Tanto had a couple
of attributes you should hold on to.

1020
01:23:34,684 --> 01:23:36,511
Wasn't so long ago you would've said:

1021
01:23:36,728 --> 01:23:39,931
"There but for the grace
of God, it's not me."

1022
01:23:41,024 --> 01:23:44,393
Quietly taking your place
in the end of the pack.

1023
01:23:45,112 --> 01:23:46,191
Where is that guy?

1024
01:23:47,197 --> 01:23:48,572
Where has he gone?

1025
01:23:49,532 --> 01:23:50,611
Who cares?

1026
01:23:51,200 --> 01:23:52,363
I do.

1027
01:23:52,577 --> 01:23:53,691
I miss him.

1028
01:23:59,667 --> 01:24:02,787
I want you to be the first to know
I'm terminating the kid's contract.

1029
01:24:03,796 --> 01:24:06,583
- Why?
- I don't think he's the real deal.

1030
01:24:07,633 --> 01:24:10,254
I don't think he's mentally
tough enough.

1031
01:24:11,762 --> 01:24:13,505
I don't think he's adult enough!

1032
01:24:13,763 --> 01:24:15,523
Getting out of a car in
the middle of a race.

1033
01:24:15,683 --> 01:24:18,256
- Saved a man's life.
- I'm not here to debate with you!

1034
01:24:19,770 --> 01:24:23,103
I'm gonna go for Brandenburg.
Next year.

1035
01:24:23,732 --> 01:24:26,305
- What are you doing Carl?
- Whatever it takes to win.

1036
01:24:27,318 --> 01:24:29,743
- Does his brother know?
- Brother's brokering the deal.

1037
01:24:29,821 --> 01:24:31,150
- Don't do this.
- It's done!

1038
01:24:31,365 --> 01:24:33,024
- Then undo it.
- Oh, you suddenly care.

1039
01:24:33,241 --> 01:24:35,613
- Don't kill him off!
- Don't kill him off?

1040
01:24:36,036 --> 01:24:37,827
I watched you kill yourself!

1041
01:24:38,746 --> 01:24:42,411
You had everything,
and you threw it all away!

1042
01:24:42,625 --> 01:24:45,579
And I had to sit there and watch!

1043
01:24:46,421 --> 01:24:49,505
The slowest man in the fastest sport.

1044
01:24:49,674 --> 01:24:54,549
I wake up every morning,
my legs are on fire.

1045
01:24:54,970 --> 01:24:59,015
I know I'm gonna have to sit
in this chair for the rest of the day.

1046
01:24:59,766 --> 01:25:03,634
But if they gave me one more chance,
I'd do it all over again.

1047
01:25:06,315 --> 01:25:07,477
It ain't gonna happen.

1048
01:25:09,026 --> 01:25:13,687
We are all damaged.

1049
01:25:17,700 --> 01:25:19,694
I've got an excuse.

1050
01:25:20,620 --> 01:25:21,949
You don't.

1051
01:25:23,290 --> 01:25:24,665
Do you?

1052
01:25:56,822 --> 01:26:00,819
I want you to know that I know
about you going out to Brandenburg.

1053
01:26:06,790 --> 01:26:08,270
Where have you been keeping yourself?

1054
01:26:08,417 --> 01:26:09,911
Meeting after meeting.

1055
01:26:10,127 --> 01:26:11,870
In fact I've got a dinner right now.

1056
01:26:12,087 --> 01:26:13,415
Catch you later?

1057
01:26:14,005 --> 01:26:16,211
- Yeah, I'll see you tomorrow.
- Okay.

1058
01:26:20,970 --> 01:26:21,970
Hello.

1059
01:26:22,681 --> 01:26:24,803
Jimmy, it's Sophia.

1060
01:26:25,225 --> 01:26:26,387
Is everything okay?

1061
01:26:28,227 --> 01:26:29,390
Something I have to tell you.

1062
01:26:35,776 --> 01:26:38,017
What restaurant did you pick?

1063
01:26:38,195 --> 01:26:41,979
Nina, you're in great hands.
You are going to love this place.

1064
01:26:42,199 --> 01:26:43,658
- Demille.
- Jimmy.

1065
01:26:44,076 --> 01:26:46,697
What are you doing here?
I'll just be a minute.

1066
01:26:49,164 --> 01:26:51,037
Please don't walk away from me.

1067
01:26:51,958 --> 01:26:53,073
Did you sell me out?

1068
01:26:53,334 --> 01:26:55,411
Are you working for Brandenburg now?

1069
01:26:56,071 --> 01:26:57,749
I think we should take this inside.

1070
01:26:57,923 --> 01:26:59,400
Why are you doing this to me, Demille?

1071
01:26:59,424 --> 01:27:01,432
Wait a minute! Who sold out who first?

1072
01:27:01,542 --> 01:27:04,361
I would never sell you out.
I would never sell out my own brother.

1073
01:27:04,396 --> 01:27:05,806
When you started listening
to everybody and stopped

1074
01:27:05,818 --> 01:27:07,099
listening to me that's
exactly what you did.

1075
01:27:07,123 --> 01:27:09,075
No Demille, I was just
trying something different.

1076
01:27:09,099 --> 01:27:11,220
For the first time in my life
I was thinking for myself.

1077
01:27:11,244 --> 01:27:11,917
What's wrong with that?

1078
01:27:11,929 --> 01:27:13,956
Speaking on your own and shutting
me out and few other things.

1079
01:27:13,980 --> 01:27:17,728
And I was with you... I was with you all
the way until you handed your mind over...

1080
01:27:17,900 --> 01:27:20,569
to that has-been.
Who got you here?

1081
01:27:20,778 --> 01:27:22,804
Who busted his ass while
you got all the glory?

1082
01:27:22,816 --> 01:27:24,727
You couldn't book a plane
ticket without me.

1083
01:27:24,948 --> 01:27:27,701
You left me, and let me
tell you something:

1084
01:27:27,868 --> 01:27:29,588
There is no worse feeling
getting someone...

1085
01:27:29,829 --> 01:27:32,236
to the top only to have them
drop you like you never existed.

1086
01:27:32,456 --> 01:27:33,950
You did that, you.

1087
01:27:34,499 --> 01:27:36,492
Ten years, Jimmy!

1088
01:27:36,668 --> 01:27:38,246
All a waste.

1089
01:27:39,129 --> 01:27:41,815
It was coming together. Demille.
Why can't you wait a bit longer?

1090
01:27:41,839 --> 01:27:43,916
Because I'm not your goddamn waiter.

1091
01:27:44,092 --> 01:27:45,503
I was your manager.

1092
01:27:45,719 --> 01:27:49,004
And I deserve better than that.
I deserve much better!

1093
01:27:49,222 --> 01:27:53,266
Now you're over, and I am not going
down in flames with you, brother.

1094
01:27:54,101 --> 01:27:56,343
That's one trip you're taking alone.

1095
01:28:29,744 --> 01:28:34,105
<i>Welcome to the Grand Prix of Detroit.
It's a beautiful sunny day for a race.</i>

1096
01:28:34,191 --> 01:28:37,842
<i>And a great race it's going to be.
After an eventful season...</i>

1097
01:28:37,977 --> 01:28:41,227
<i>this comes down
to championship time.</i>

1098
01:28:48,113 --> 01:28:50,105
<i>Everything's set.
Let's get this thing signed.</i>

1099
01:28:50,323 --> 01:28:52,992
After the race it's gonna be a madhouse.
What do you say?

1100
01:28:53,242 --> 01:28:54,653
I say let's hear what she says.

1101
01:28:54,869 --> 01:28:56,327
What's her idea?

1102
01:28:56,537 --> 01:28:59,158
Her idea? What do you mean her idea?

1103
01:28:59,414 --> 01:29:00,873
How does it feel?

1104
01:29:01,083 --> 01:29:03,372
What? How does what feel?

1105
01:29:04,712 --> 01:29:06,123
To be used.

1106
01:29:06,380 --> 01:29:08,503
What, I didn't treat you with manners?

1107
01:29:08,674 --> 01:29:10,713
You're gonna blow this over that?

1108
01:29:11,343 --> 01:29:14,842
Look. What do you want to do? Hit me?
Would that make you feel better?

1109
01:29:16,097 --> 01:29:18,422
- Hurting.
- A little.

1110
01:29:19,518 --> 01:29:20,929
Didn't hurt.

1111
01:29:22,813 --> 01:29:23,975
Call that a punch?

1112
01:30:05,803 --> 01:30:06,803
Did you know?

1113
01:30:06,979 --> 01:30:09,187
- Know what?
- Know about my brother?

1114
01:30:09,399 --> 01:30:10,728
Yeah, I knew.

1115
01:30:10,901 --> 01:30:12,443
You could've told me.

1116
01:30:12,819 --> 01:30:14,846
Well, I hoped you guys
could work things out.

1117
01:30:15,129 --> 01:30:16,589
He was right, you know.

1118
01:30:17,240 --> 01:30:19,000
I never even know how
to book a plane ticket.

1119
01:30:19,033 --> 01:30:21,322
Remember I said by the end of this
season, maybe you'll be on top

1120
01:30:21,334 --> 01:30:23,774
or maybe you won't. But you're
gonna know what you're made of?

1121
01:30:23,980 --> 01:30:25,658
It's the end of the season.

1122
01:30:26,666 --> 01:30:28,125
It's up to you.

1123
01:30:33,380 --> 01:30:34,958
Carl, you have to let me race.

1124
01:30:35,174 --> 01:30:36,205
I can win.

1125
01:30:36,466 --> 01:30:40,983
Look, any driver that can't get out of
the car in five seconds isn't allow to run.

1126
01:30:41,097 --> 01:30:43,528
Still trying to prove you're
better than I think you are?

1127
01:30:43,974 --> 01:30:45,172
Yeah.

1128
01:30:48,437 --> 01:30:49,437
Time him.

1129
01:31:07,288 --> 01:31:08,782
Ready?

1130
01:31:10,249 --> 01:31:11,412
Go!

1131
01:31:16,964 --> 01:31:19,004
- Four seconds.
- Great.

1132
01:31:20,301 --> 01:31:21,301
Not bad.

1133
01:31:23,053 --> 01:31:25,010
Now the vertical test.

1134
01:31:25,889 --> 01:31:27,799
Carl, don't push it.

1135
01:31:28,017 --> 01:31:29,844
The vertical test.

1136
01:31:30,019 --> 01:31:34,016
You jump up and down
on the bad foot 10 times...

1137
01:31:34,148 --> 01:31:36,187
just to see if you can handle
the pressure.

1138
01:31:37,067 --> 01:31:39,522
Again, my rules.

1139
01:31:40,945 --> 01:31:41,977
Don't glare, Joe.

1140
01:31:42,947 --> 01:31:44,442
Makes your eyes look small.

1141
01:31:44,825 --> 01:31:46,734
It's all about commitment, right?

1142
01:31:47,369 --> 01:31:48,448
- Right.
- Right.

1143
01:31:49,037 --> 01:31:51,195
All right, Jimmy. One.

1144
01:31:52,749 --> 01:31:54,207
Two.

1145
01:31:58,462 --> 01:31:59,626
Three.

1146
01:32:05,052 --> 01:32:06,084
Four.

1147
01:32:07,638 --> 01:32:08,753
Five. Come on.

1148
01:32:08,931 --> 01:32:11,054
Six. Come on, Jimmy.
Seven. Come on.

1149
01:32:11,308 --> 01:32:13,716
Eight. Nine. Ten.

1150
01:32:13,936 --> 01:32:15,264
- Yeah!
- Good.

1151
01:32:20,276 --> 01:32:22,849
Too bad you didn't try
that hard sooner.

1152
01:32:31,704 --> 01:32:33,411
<i>There are 100 laps...</i>

1153
01:32:33,580 --> 01:32:37,743
<i>200 miles between this race
and a champion.</i>

1154
01:33:00,439 --> 01:33:01,719
Bye-bye, Daddy.

1155
01:33:04,610 --> 01:33:06,069
Bye, Lucas.

1156
01:33:36,433 --> 01:33:40,017
<i>Going into this race, Beau
Brandenburg probably was thinking...</i>

1157
01:33:40,127 --> 01:33:41,886
<i>he was the winner
of the championship.</i>

1158
01:33:42,146 --> 01:33:45,515
<i>He was four points ahead, and Bly
looked like he was out of the running.</i>

1159
01:33:45,691 --> 01:33:49,111
<i>And we've just received word
that Jimmy Bly will be driving...</i>

1160
01:33:49,144 --> 01:33:53,274
<i>which is amazing news after
his injury he suffered in Germany.</i>

1161
01:33:53,616 --> 01:33:58,159
<i>So as it stands,
if Jimmy Bly wins this race...</i>

1162
01:33:58,328 --> 01:34:00,368
<i>he will become
the new world champion.</i>

1163
01:34:02,999 --> 01:34:04,031
So why'd you do it?

1164
01:34:05,752 --> 01:34:09,168
You helped me.
I thought maybe I could help you.

1165
01:34:13,343 --> 01:34:15,382
- Well, I appreciate it.
- It's okay.

1166
01:34:15,553 --> 01:34:17,012
Don't go too fast.

1167
01:34:20,683 --> 01:34:22,903
You guys take care.
Appreciate you coming.

1168
01:34:22,938 --> 01:34:24,637
Take care of yourself.

1169
01:34:24,896 --> 01:34:29,723
<i>Jimmy Bly is a hero today, along with
Joe Tanto and Beau Brandenburg...</i>

1170
01:34:29,884 --> 01:34:33,304
<i>who all got to the scene
of Memo Moreno's horrific crash...</i>

1171
01:34:33,420 --> 01:34:36,606
<i>which had his car upside down in the water.
He was about to drown.</i>

1172
01:34:36,824 --> 01:34:39,649
<i>These men, they jumped in,
got him out of the water...</i>

1173
01:34:39,768 --> 01:34:42,781
<i>before a big explosion
consumed the entire area.</i>

1174
01:34:44,665 --> 01:34:48,912
You know that if I lose this race,
I'm going to blame it on you.

1175
01:34:49,503 --> 01:34:51,329
That's what I'm here for.

1176
01:34:51,630 --> 01:34:52,958
I love you.

1177
01:34:53,381 --> 01:34:54,496
I love you too.

1178
01:36:18,214 --> 01:36:21,629
<i>Gentlemen! Start your engines!</i>

1179
01:36:25,012 --> 01:36:26,928
<i>Let's look at the starting grid.</i>

1180
01:36:26,972 --> 01:36:29,095
<i>We have Beau Brandenburg
in the pole position.</i>

1181
01:36:29,307 --> 01:36:31,098
<i>Gidley will be following him.</i>

1182
01:36:32,227 --> 01:36:34,550
<i>Joe Tanto in the Nextel car.
He starts at 10th.</i>

1183
01:36:36,440 --> 01:36:38,598
<i>Jimmy Bly is starting
in the 26th pole position.</i>

1184
01:36:38,817 --> 01:36:40,015
He didn't qualify today.

1185
01:36:40,276 --> 01:36:43,230
<i>He's got 100 laps to catch
Beau Brandenburg...</i>

1186
01:36:43,488 --> 01:36:45,776
<i>if he wants to become this year's
world champion.</i>

1187
01:37:11,890 --> 01:37:14,844
<i>We're off to a good start
here in Detroit.</i>

1188
01:37:16,811 --> 01:37:19,018
<i>Brandenburg's jumped out in front.</i>

1189
01:37:19,189 --> 01:37:21,063
<i>Woh! Trouble!</i>

1190
01:37:31,200 --> 01:37:34,367
<i>Tanto's caught in traffic.
He doesn't have anyplace to go!</i>

1191
01:37:37,707 --> 01:37:40,494
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
we are under a yellow flag...</i>

1192
01:37:40,752 --> 01:37:42,376
<i>until the cars can be removed.</i>

1193
01:37:42,545 --> 01:37:45,665
<i>Joe Tanto is in the pit
with a broken front wing.</i>

1194
01:37:45,840 --> 01:37:47,547
<i>What's the story on Tanto?</i>

1195
01:37:47,758 --> 01:37:49,834
Tanto is out of it.
Don't worry about Tanto.

1196
01:37:50,427 --> 01:37:51,838
<i>Got it. That's too bad.</i>

1197
01:37:52,346 --> 01:37:53,509
<i>Come on. Come on!</i>

1198
01:37:53,723 --> 01:37:57,506
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
we have just one lap until green.</i>

1199
01:38:00,562 --> 01:38:01,760
Go, go, go!

1200
01:38:07,110 --> 01:38:10,978
<i>A fast pit stop for the Nextel team,
but this unfortunate mishap...</i>

1201
01:38:11,156 --> 01:38:13,398
<i>is going to drop Tanto
to last place...</i>

1202
01:38:13,617 --> 01:38:16,534
<i>right behind his teammate,
Jimmy Bly.</i>

1203
01:38:18,329 --> 01:38:19,823
So, Jimmy, what do you think?

1204
01:38:20,707 --> 01:38:22,117
It's not looking too good.

1205
01:38:22,917 --> 01:38:24,157
We can work a way through this.

1206
01:38:24,460 --> 01:38:25,460
You think so?

1207
01:38:25,795 --> 01:38:28,120
I know we can if we stay tight
and stay close.

1208
01:38:28,548 --> 01:38:29,923
Okay. Let's do it.

1209
01:38:30,300 --> 01:38:32,506
<i>Green flag comes out again.</i>

1210
01:38:38,265 --> 01:38:39,973
<i>I'll take it right, you cut left.</i>

1211
01:38:40,475 --> 01:38:43,512
<i>Look at this amazing teamwork
between Bly and Tanto!</i>

1212
01:38:44,397 --> 01:38:46,887
Hey, Joe, not bad for an old-timer.

1213
01:38:47,107 --> 01:38:49,100
That's it. Every man for himself.

1214
01:38:53,113 --> 01:38:54,144
Hey, not so fast.

1215
01:38:56,407 --> 01:38:58,484
<i>Who wants to be in front
of the other?</i>

1216
01:38:58,660 --> 01:39:00,119
What the hell are you two doing?

1217
01:39:00,787 --> 01:39:02,246
Back off, back off.

1218
01:39:02,456 --> 01:39:04,016
Don't get it kid.
Don't be afraid of me.

1219
01:39:04,249 --> 01:39:06,169
Now why would I be afraid
of an old guy like you?

1220
01:39:06,417 --> 01:39:08,624
Carl, let Joe race his race.

1221
01:39:08,836 --> 01:39:10,247
Thanks, kid. I appreciate that.

1222
01:39:12,590 --> 01:39:15,461
Let's split them at the turn.
I'll take the inside.

1223
01:39:15,802 --> 01:39:17,510
Again they split around another car!

1224
01:39:17,762 --> 01:39:21,501
<i>As they battle, it brings both
cars forward through the field.</i>

1225
01:39:24,185 --> 01:39:25,643
Pass me on the left, Jimmy.

1226
01:39:28,897 --> 01:39:30,096
Way to go.

1227
01:39:30,566 --> 01:39:34,016
<i>Tanto and Bly are double-teaming
the entire field.</i>

1228
01:39:34,144 --> 01:39:35,937
<i>What an incredible display of driving!</i>

1229
01:39:40,158 --> 01:39:42,413
Come on, what are you doing?
Don't stop now.

1230
01:39:42,425 --> 01:39:43,776
Stopping? Who's stopping?

1231
01:39:45,914 --> 01:39:48,452
<i>We are now halfway
to the checkered flag.</i>

1232
01:39:48,792 --> 01:39:50,666
Okay, Joe. Try to keep up.

1233
01:39:56,924 --> 01:39:57,753
Still back there, Joe?

1234
01:39:57,809 --> 01:40:00,832
- Thanks for asking. I'm still here.
- I'm impressed.

1235
01:40:05,517 --> 01:40:08,434
<i>Bly passes and Tanto
is following suit.</i>

1236
01:40:11,355 --> 01:40:15,566
<i>With just 20 laps to go, Jimmy Bly
has just moved into seventh place...</i>

1237
01:40:15,776 --> 01:40:18,268
<i>and teammate
Joe Tanto is in sixth.</i>

1238
01:40:18,488 --> 01:40:19,819
<i>Everybody's off the pace.</i>

1239
01:40:19,939 --> 01:40:21,815
<i>But Bly and Tanto
are coming on strong.</i>

1240
01:40:21,991 --> 01:40:23,697
<i>Beau Brandenburg is still in the lead.</i>

1241
01:40:23,732 --> 01:40:26,741
<i>In second place is Alex Barron.
Barron has an engine go!</i>

1242
01:40:27,663 --> 01:40:30,070
<i>Two cars swerving to miss the oil!</i>

1243
01:40:30,290 --> 01:40:34,335
<i>Car up over the wall!
Several cars involved!</i>

1244
01:40:37,464 --> 01:40:41,164
<i>Here comes Jimmy Bly.
He closes on the accident.</i>

1245
01:40:47,515 --> 01:40:49,473
<i>Bly has nowhere to go.</i>

1246
01:40:57,275 --> 01:41:01,023
<i>As the smoke clears Bly and Tanto find
themselves in second and third...</i>

1247
01:41:01,237 --> 01:41:02,612
<i>behind Beau Brandenburg.</i>

1248
01:41:03,322 --> 01:41:06,988
<i>The drivers are gonna take advantage
now of this full-course caution...</i>

1249
01:41:07,243 --> 01:41:10,991
<i>and enter the pits
for the last time this season.</i>

1250
01:41:13,373 --> 01:41:18,000
<i>Brandenburg, Bly and Tanto all are
completing very fast pit stops.</i>

1251
01:41:19,446 --> 01:41:24,089
<i>With 10 laps to go,
Beau Brandenburg is in first place...</i>

1252
01:41:24,301 --> 01:41:28,381
<i>Jimmy Bly is in second,
and Joe Tanto is in third place.</i>

1253
01:41:30,473 --> 01:41:34,886
<i>The world championship comes down
to these last 10 laps.</i>

1254
01:41:38,523 --> 01:41:40,848
Alright Jimmy, show them
what you're made of, kid.

1255
01:41:41,234 --> 01:41:42,479
Okay, Joe.

1256
01:41:43,069 --> 01:41:44,184
<i>Green flag!</i>

1257
01:41:45,238 --> 01:41:46,336
<i>We're back to racing!</i>

1258
01:41:46,356 --> 01:41:49,063
<i>It's a sprint now to the finish
and the championship.</i>

1259
01:41:53,913 --> 01:41:57,831
<i>Bly is right on Brandenburg's tail.
He wants that championship.</i>

1260
01:41:57,950 --> 01:41:59,908
<i>Take him now. Make your move.</i>

1261
01:42:01,336 --> 01:42:04,835
<i>He comes alongside Brandenburg.
Brandenburg cuts him off!</i>

1262
01:42:08,259 --> 01:42:09,588
<i>Bly is gonna try it again.</i>

1263
01:42:09,845 --> 01:42:13,090
<i>He cuts and ducks inside of Bly!
He has the lead!</i>

1264
01:42:13,125 --> 01:42:16,096
<i>Jimmy Bly has just taken the lead.</i>

1265
01:42:17,560 --> 01:42:20,230
<i>Bly gets past Brandenburg.
He's in the lead.</i>

1266
01:42:20,438 --> 01:42:22,763
<i>Great driving by Bly.</i>

1267
01:42:24,959 --> 01:42:27,567
<i>Brandenburg won't let Bly
get away that easily.</i>

1268
01:42:27,729 --> 01:42:29,402
<i>I'll pull him back in. There's time.</i>

1269
01:42:30,740 --> 01:42:33,347
<i>Brandenburg is really putting
pressure on Bly.</i>

1270
01:42:33,467 --> 01:42:34,482
Don't overreach, kid.

1271
01:42:34,702 --> 01:42:37,903
Just four laps to go and you are
the world champion.

1272
01:42:39,081 --> 01:42:40,575
<i>He's losing it.</i>

1273
01:42:41,751 --> 01:42:42,751
<i>Come on, Jimmy!</i>

1274
01:42:42,835 --> 01:42:46,619
<i>Oh Bly may be in trouble.
He weaves back and forth.</i>

1275
01:42:46,797 --> 01:42:49,917
<i>Brandenburg is right there,
ready to get past him.</i>

1276
01:42:57,015 --> 01:42:59,589
<i>And Brandenburg goes to the lead!</i>

1277
01:43:07,275 --> 01:43:08,473
Nice while it lasted.

1278
01:43:09,986 --> 01:43:13,879
<i>Jimmy Bly loses the lead
with just three laps to go.</i>

1279
01:43:13,880 --> 01:43:14,547
He tried.

1280
01:43:14,548 --> 01:43:18,653
<i>This is something we've seen
this young rookie do so many times.</i>

1281
01:43:18,828 --> 01:43:21,745
<i>Carl Henry has got
to be disappointed.</i>

1282
01:43:27,211 --> 01:43:29,832
- What is he doing?
- Jesus.

1283
01:43:30,506 --> 01:43:31,538
He's back.

1284
01:43:35,302 --> 01:43:39,469
<i>Now, Joe Tanto making a move.
He comes up alongside Jimmy Bly.</i>

1285
01:43:39,631 --> 01:43:42,183
<i>He passes him! Tanto to second.</i>

1286
01:43:42,893 --> 01:43:44,885
<i>They're shoving and elbowing
each other.</i>

1287
01:43:45,270 --> 01:43:48,224
<i>Brandenburg, Tanto, Bly.
One, two, three.</i>

1288
01:43:54,612 --> 01:43:56,569
<i>We've got one lap to go.</i>

1289
01:43:56,781 --> 01:43:57,944
Let's do it.

1290
01:44:10,086 --> 01:44:13,537
<i>Joe Tanto has taken the lead!</i>

1291
01:44:13,756 --> 01:44:15,131
Unbelievable.

1292
01:44:16,467 --> 01:44:18,127
It's incredible. I can't believe it.

1293
01:44:18,344 --> 01:44:20,716
<i>But problems with Tanto's car!</i>

1294
01:44:20,888 --> 01:44:22,596
<i>Tanto's in trouble.</i>

1295
01:44:24,308 --> 01:44:25,308
Will it hold together?

1296
01:44:26,101 --> 01:44:27,216
No, not for long.

1297
01:44:27,477 --> 01:44:28,917
- Hang on, Joe.
- Stay in there, Joe.

1298
01:44:29,104 --> 01:44:33,393
<i>What's Tanto doing? He ought to park
that thing but he stays out in front!</i>

1299
01:44:33,428 --> 01:44:35,349
I can't hold it together!
Take it, Jimmy!

1300
01:44:38,280 --> 01:44:40,023
<i>They split him!</i>

1301
01:44:40,407 --> 01:44:41,486
He's lifting off!

1302
01:44:41,658 --> 01:44:43,615
I see that. He had it!

1303
01:44:43,827 --> 01:44:48,572
<i>Tanto has removed himself from
the race, leaving Brandenburg and Bly.</i>

1304
01:44:48,956 --> 01:44:53,960
<i>Neck and neck down the homestretch,
battling for the world championship.</i>

1305
01:45:10,811 --> 01:45:14,761
<i>Jimmy, just drive because you
love it. Drive for pure victory.</i>

1306
01:45:21,363 --> 01:45:22,906
He's humming.

1307
01:45:26,618 --> 01:45:27,863
Thanks for going, Jimmy.

1308
01:45:28,203 --> 01:45:30,445
Pure victory. You're right there.

1309
01:45:32,540 --> 01:45:36,538
<i>Suddenly, Jimmy Bly seems
to have a renewed vigor.</i>

1310
01:45:43,426 --> 01:45:44,920
You'll buckle! Back it down!

1311
01:45:45,136 --> 01:45:47,805
<i>Tanto's suspension has broken.
He's now spinning.</i>

1312
01:45:48,014 --> 01:45:51,076
<i>But the battle is up front
for the checkered flag!</i>

1313
01:45:57,690 --> 01:46:00,525
<i>Here it comes.
Right down the finish.</i>

1314
01:46:02,611 --> 01:46:03,804
<i>Bly takes it!</i>

1315
01:46:03,816 --> 01:46:07,189
<i>Jimmy Bly wins the
world championship!</i>

1316
01:46:07,824 --> 01:46:12,950
<i>Beau Brandenburg finishes second,
and Joe Tanto finishes third.</i>

1317
01:46:17,000 --> 01:46:20,499
<i>Following by Brandenburg... Tanto spinning
across the finish for third place.</i>

1318
01:46:20,670 --> 01:46:25,213
<i>I'll say, the Hummer has taught
us all something here today in Detroit.</i>

1319
01:46:25,424 --> 01:46:26,884
They're gonna kill me.

1320
01:46:46,112 --> 01:46:47,440
Joseph.

1321
01:46:48,864 --> 01:46:51,320
- You could've won that race, couldn't you?
- I did win.

1322
01:46:52,326 --> 01:46:53,571
Thanks.

1323
01:47:07,549 --> 01:47:09,091
Hey, you were incredible.

1324
01:47:09,300 --> 01:47:12,052
I know. I lost because of her.

1325
01:47:18,309 --> 01:47:21,310
This year's champion, Jimmy Bly!

1326
01:47:41,832 --> 01:47:44,120
Luc! Glad you stuck around.

1327
01:47:45,710 --> 01:47:47,704
You were really something out there.

1328
01:47:47,922 --> 01:47:49,831
Beau Brandenburg!

1329
01:48:04,312 --> 01:48:06,803
Go on, you're missing
your celebration.

1330
01:48:07,482 --> 01:48:09,309
Don't you go anywhere.

1331
01:48:09,567 --> 01:48:11,145
Come on, go!

1332
01:48:21,496 --> 01:48:24,895
And finally, our third finisher...

1333
01:48:24,949 --> 01:48:26,447
Joe Tanto!

1334
01:48:32,005 --> 01:48:34,163
Jimmy! Jimmy, you did it, man.

1335
01:48:37,720 --> 01:48:39,156
Thanks for everything.

1336
01:48:39,546 --> 01:48:42,843
I tell you what. You owe your brother too.
Whatever button he pushed got you going.

1337
01:48:43,016 --> 01:48:45,642
And listen, enjoy this.
It doesn't last long.


